&lt;p&gt;The series follows Manas, a young man who discovers his extraordinary destiny tied to the Mahabharata, as he embarks on a journey to restore the sacred Saraswati River and confront dark forces threatening the world.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;You can find it on Amazon Kindle, and it's also available with Kindle Unlimited!&lt;/p&gt;




&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Thanks for reading! Feel free to reach out if you have any questions or want to discuss tech, books, or anything in between.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;I've started out programming as a teen who just wanted to create scripts that would&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;do cool and useful stuff. Throughout some time I was learning web dev and making personal side projects. The time was passing and I was getting better at coding. But one day and after that more and more often I started getting burned out, I could not program anything, I did not feel the fire of it. Some time has passed and when I thought I was recovered and excited about stuff again I've hit one more burnout and some time later hit it once again. &lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;And now I'm sitting here and thinking how to escape my current burnout.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Would be glad to hear other experience in such situations.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;P.S. I suppose my burnouts were caused by just not having concrete goals, my whole goal was to build things for myself or get a job (though getting a job did not excite me that much, just because I probably will not find purpose in doing for something I don't see potential in, at least on an average job).&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;P.P.S. When AI started to do really well in coding, the situation has worsened as I did not enjoy "AI coding" that much.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;App store screenshots all look the same: a beautiful portrait, a witty opening line, a promise of "lifelike conversations." None of that tells you how a character behaves on message twenty, when you change your mind about the scene, or when you set a boundary. The only way to find out is to try it.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The good news is that you don't need a week. A focused 15-minute session with a handful of deliberate prompts will tell you most of what you need to know. Below are seven test prompts I use whenever I try a new app, along with what to watch for and a simple scoring rubric so you can compare apps side by side instead of relying on a vague impression.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;A quick note before you start: AI replies vary. Run each prompt once or twice, judge the pattern rather than a single line, and never use real personal information as test material. Fictional details work just as well.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


Before you begin: set up a fair test
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Pick one character per app that fits the kind of conversation you actually want, whether that is a fantasy adventure, a slow-burn romance, or a casual chat with a sarcastic roommate. Comparing a cozy bookshop owner in one app with a battle-hardened knight in another tells you about the characters, not the apps.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Then open a notes file. For each prompt, jot down a score from 0 to 2 and one sentence about why. That's it.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


Prompt 1: The specific opener (minute 0 to 2)
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Try:&lt;/strong&gt; Write a first message that refers to something concrete in the character's profile or opening scene. For example: "You said the lighthouse lamp went out last night. Did you find out why?"&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What it reveals:&lt;/strong&gt; Whether the character's setup is clear enough to build on, and whether the reply picks up your detail or ignores it in favor of a generic greeting.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Score:&lt;/strong&gt; 2 if the reply engages with your specific detail and adds something new. 1 if it acknowledges it vaguely. 0 if it resets to a canned intro.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


Prompt 2: The neutral personality probe (minute 2 to 4)
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Try:&lt;/strong&gt; Ask something that has no "correct" answer: "What would you do with an unexpected free afternoon?"&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What it reveals:&lt;/strong&gt; Voice. A grumpy alchemist and a cheerful courier should not answer the same way. Look at vocabulary, rhythm, priorities, and humor. If you have time, ask a second character the same question and compare.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Score:&lt;/strong&gt; 2 if the answer clearly sounds like this character and nobody else. 1 if it is pleasant but generic. 0 if it breaks character or sounds like a customer support bot.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


Prompt 3: The planted detail (minute 4 to 6)
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Try:&lt;/strong&gt; Drop in one harmless fictional fact early: "By the way, I'm carrying my grandmother's brass compass. It always points slightly east." Chat about something else for a few messages.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What it reveals:&lt;/strong&gt; Short-term context handling. You'll check on this detail in Prompt 5.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Score:&lt;/strong&gt; No score yet. Just note exactly what you planted.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


Prompt 4: The steering wheel (minute 6 to 8)
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Try:&lt;/strong&gt; Change direction politely and explicitly: "Let's leave the market and head somewhere quiet. Keep things light, and let me decide what my character does."&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What it reveals:&lt;/strong&gt; Whether the app respects your role in the story. Strong characters follow the new direction and leave you room to act. Weak ones keep going with their previous script, or start narrating your thoughts and decisions for you.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Score:&lt;/strong&gt; 2 if it follows the new direction and leaves your choices to you. 1 if it follows but takes over your character. 0 if it ignores the request.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


Prompt 5: The correction test (minute 8 to 10)
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Try:&lt;/strong&gt; Refer back to your planted detail, slightly wrong on purpose, or correct a mistake the character made: "Wait, the compass points west, doesn't it? No, sorry, east. Let's keep going."&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What it reveals:&lt;/strong&gt; How well the conversation recovers. Does it adopt the correction smoothly, or does the story get muddled? This is one of the clearest signals of how frustrating long roleplays will feel.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Score:&lt;/strong&gt; 2 if it remembers the original detail and handles the correction gracefully. 1 if it needs the correction but then gets it right. 0 if it stays confused.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Remember that a 15-minute test only shows how this particular exchange behaved. It does not prove long-term or cross-session memory, so treat any "memory" marketing claims as something to check in the app's own documentation.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


Prompt 6: The boundary check (minute 10 to 12)
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Try:&lt;/strong&gt; State a clear, reasonable boundary: "I'd rather not include violence in this story. Can we keep the tension emotional instead?" Then continue the scene for a few messages.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What it reveals:&lt;/strong&gt; Safety and respect. A good experience honors the request without lecturing you and without quietly drifting back. This prompt is not a substitute for the app's actual safety settings, so also look for content controls, reporting tools, and age requirements in the settings or policy pages.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Score:&lt;/strong&gt; 2 if the boundary holds naturally. 1 if it holds but feels clunky or preachy. 0 if it is ignored.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


Prompt 7: The comeback (minute 12 to 15)
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Try:&lt;/strong&gt; Close the app, wait a few minutes, then find your way back to the same character and conversation. Send: "Sorry, I got distracted. Where were we?"&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What it reveals:&lt;/strong&gt; The return experience. Can you find the character again easily? Is there enough context on screen to pick up the thread? Some apps also show character posts or updates that give you a fresh opening line, which can make returning feel less like restarting.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Score:&lt;/strong&gt; 2 if returning is easy and the conversation continues naturally. 1 if you need to remind it of the scene. 0 if the thread is hard to find or the character behaves like a stranger.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


The scoring rubric
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Add up your scores. Prompt 3 is a setup step, so the maximum is 12.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="table-wrapper-paragraph"&gt;&lt;table&gt;
&lt;thead&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;th&gt;Score&lt;/th&gt;
&lt;th&gt;What it usually means&lt;/th&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;/thead&gt;
&lt;tbody&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;10 to 12&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Strong fit. Worth checking pricing and privacy next.&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;7 to 9&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Promising, with one or two weak spots. Decide whether they matter for your style.&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;4 to 6&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Usable for short, casual chats; likely frustrating for long stories.&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;0 to 3&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Probably not for you, at least with this character. Try one more before giving up.&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;/tbody&gt;
&lt;/table&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Weight the prompts that match your priorities. If you write long campaigns, Prompts 3 and 5 count double. If you want comfortable, low-stakes conversation, Prompts 2 and 7 matter most. If you share the app with boundaries you care about, Prompt 6 is a pass/fail gate.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


What the 15 minutes won't tell you
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Some things can't be tested in a chat window. Before you subscribe, read the current pricing page: what the free tier includes, whether there are usage limits, and how cancellation works. Read the privacy policy too, especially how chats are stored and whether you can delete them. Check that the service is available in your region and language. These practical details are separate from how good the writing is, and they're often what decides whether you stay.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


Putting it together
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Run the same seven prompts across three or four apps and you'll have a real comparison instead of a gut feeling. If you need a starting shortlist, this guide to &lt;a href="https://pogee.ai/hub/en/blog/best-ai-character-chat-apps" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;ai character chat apps&lt;/a&gt; walks through how to choose by the kind of conversation you want, which pairs well with the scores you just collected.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;If you're coming from one platform and want to see how others compare, the same rubric works for evaluating &lt;a href="https://pogee.ai/hub/en/blog/best-ai-character-chat-apps" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;character ai alternatives&lt;/a&gt;: keep the character type constant, run the prompts, and let the numbers argue for you.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;For Prompt 7 in particular, it's worth including at least one app built around a character's world beyond the chat box. &lt;a href="https://pogee.ai/en/" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;Pogee&lt;/a&gt;, for example, offers character profiles, search, and daily moments you can browse before you start a conversation, which gives the comeback test something extra to work with.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Fifteen minutes, seven prompts, one honest score. It's a small investment that can save you weeks with the wrong app, and it makes finding the &lt;a href="https://pogee.ai/hub/en/blog/best-ai-character-chat-apps" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;best AI character chat apps&lt;/a&gt; for your own style a lot less of a guessing game.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h1&gt;


CVE-2026-44265: Code and SQL Injection via Programmatic AST Emission in @enspirit/elo
&lt;/h1&gt;

&lt;blockquote&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Vulnerability ID:&lt;/strong&gt; CVE-2026-44265&lt;br&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;CVSS Score:&lt;/strong&gt; 7.4&lt;br&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Published:&lt;/strong&gt; 2026-11-03&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/blockquote&gt;

&lt;p&gt;A code injection and SQL injection vulnerability exists in @enspirit/elo prior to version 1.0.1. When compiling expressions via the programmatic Abstract Syntax Tree (AST) API, the backend emitters for JavaScript, Ruby, Python, and PostgreSQL SQL fail to perform runtime type validation or lexical verification on AST node properties. Applications that construct or deserialize AST nodes from untrusted sources allow attackers to inject arbitrary code or SQL commands directly into the emitted target output.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


TL;DR
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Elo compiler backends (@enspirit/elo &amp;lt; 1.0.1) interpolate programmatic AST node properties directly into generated JavaScript, Python, Ruby, and SQL code without runtime validation, enabling Remote Code Execution (RCE) and SQL Injection when untrusted AST structures are compiled.&lt;/p&gt;




&lt;h3&gt;


⚠️ Exploit Status: POC
&lt;/h3&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


Technical Details
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;CVE ID&lt;/strong&gt;: CVE-2026-44265 (GHSA-x9rp-7wh3-2rj5)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Primary CWE&lt;/strong&gt;: CWE-94 (Code Injection) / CWE-89 (SQL Injection)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;CVSS v3.1 Score&lt;/strong&gt;: 7.4 High (CVSS:3.1/AV:L/AC:H/PR:N/UI:N/S:U/C:H/I:H/A:H)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Affected Component&lt;/strong&gt;: @enspirit/elo (&amp;lt; 1.0.1) Compiler Backends&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Patched Version&lt;/strong&gt;: 1.0.1&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Impact&lt;/strong&gt;: Remote Code Execution (JS, Python, Ruby) &amp;amp; SQL Injection (PostgreSQL)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Exploit Status&lt;/strong&gt;: Proof of Concept (PoC) Available&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;CISA KEV Status&lt;/strong&gt;: Not Listed&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


Affected Systems
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;@enspirit/elo (npm package)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;@enspirit/elo&lt;/strong&gt;: &amp;lt; 1.0.1 (Fixed in: &lt;code&gt;1.0.1&lt;/code&gt;)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


Code Analysis
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;h3&gt;


Commit: &lt;a href="https://github.com/enspirit/elo/commit/fb57dd37a2669d9c412454225c5b89a2adba5d93" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;fb57dd3&lt;/a&gt;
&lt;/h3&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Validate identifier and numeric-literal IR nodes to prevent AST-API injection&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h3&gt;


Commit: &lt;a href="https://github.com/enspirit/elo/commit/d2a89a8db76a244eb740687524a7e8529b7554b5" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;d2a89a8&lt;/a&gt;
&lt;/h3&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Release v1.0.1&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


Mitigation Strategies
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Upgrade @enspirit/elo to version 1.0.1 or later to enforce built-in runtime AST validation.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Validate all deserialized JSON or external AST structures using a runtime schema validator (e.g., Zod, Ajv) prior to invoking Elo compiler functions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Avoid exposing programmatic AST compilation endpoints directly to client-submitted JSON; prefer parsing raw Elo expression strings through the standard parser.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Execute dynamically compiled JavaScript, Python, or Ruby code within isolated sandboxes and run generated SQL queries using least-privilege database roles.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Remediation Steps:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;ol&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Update package.json to require "@enspirit/elo": "^1.0.1" and run npm install or yarn upgrade.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Audit application code for any direct calls to compileToJavaScript, compileToPython, compileToRuby, or compileToSQL that accept externally constructed AST objects.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Implement try/catch blocks around compilation calls to handle validation errors thrown when malformed AST nodes are encountered.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ol&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


References
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href="https://github.com/enspirit/elo/security/advisories/GHSA-x9rp-7wh3-2rj5" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;GitHub Security Advisory: GHSA-x9rp-7wh3-2rj5&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href="https://github.com/enspirit/elo/commit/fb57dd37a2669d9c412454225c5b89a2adba5d93" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;Patch Commit: Validate identifier and numeric-literal IR nodes&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href="https://github.com/enspirit/elo/commit/d2a89a8db76a244eb740687524a7e8529b7554b5" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;Release Commit: v1.0.1&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href="https://www.cve.org/CVERecord?id=CVE-2026-44265" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;CVE-2026-44265 Record&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href="https://github.com/enspirit/elo" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;Elo GitHub Repository&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;




&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;&lt;a href="https://cvereports.com/reports/CVE-2026-44265" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;Read the full report for CVE-2026-44265 on our website&lt;/a&gt; for more details including interactive diagrams and full exploit analysis.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;After the browser produced a verified document-backed answer, the next requirement was a phone application that could demonstrate the integration without repeated deployment windows and several logins.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The agreed target was Ionic React on a Pixel 6 Pro running Android 17, delivered directly as an APK. The owner wanted a remembered 30-day enrollment, fingerprint unlock, a new chat on every entry and access to supported documents inside the existing approved SharePoint site.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;This article describes both the implemented design and its current verification boundary. The native device-test build passed owner-observed fingerprint and background-clearing checks. The live v5 APK is installed and distributed, and the backend is deployed. Live mobile sign-in is still under investigation: tapping Sign in has not yet been observed to redirect successfully to PF. There is no claim of completed mobile Copilot acceptance.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


Step 1: Separate the mobile project from the server
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The Ionic application lives under &lt;code&gt;apps/mobile&lt;/code&gt; with its own package and Android build. It does not add its UI dependencies to the dependency-light simulation.&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight plaintext"&gt;&lt;code&gt;apps/mobile/
src/                 React UI, controller and fixed HTTPS transport
tests/               Lifecycle, transport and proof tests
android/             Capacitor application and native plugins
scripts/             Local Android build helper
src/mobile/            Server-side enrollment and execution components
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;There are two explicit build modes. The default is a labelled offline device test. The &lt;code&gt;live&lt;/code&gt; mode uses the fixed agent API and never returns a local success message when real services fail.&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight powershell"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="c"&gt;# Run from apps/mobile after installing its pinned dependencies.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="w"&gt;
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;npm&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="w"&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;test&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="w"&gt;
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nv"&gt;$&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nn"&gt;env&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nv"&gt;VITE_MOBILE_MODE&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="w"&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="w"&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s1"&gt;'live'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="w"&gt;
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;npm&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="w"&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;run&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="w"&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;android:build&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="w"&gt;
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;The repository helper checks the configured JDK and SDK, builds the web application, synchronizes Capacitor and runs native assembly, unit tests and lint. It signs with a dedicated local demo key outside source control. That key is a distribution credential, not a PF, Graph or agent credential.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


Step 2: Make fingerprint unlock cryptographic
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;A JavaScript flag such as &lt;code&gt;authenticated: true&lt;/code&gt; is insufficient evidence for resuming a delegated session. We implemented a small native boundary that creates an authentication-bound P-256 Android Keystore key and signs a challenge through a strong biometric &lt;code&gt;CryptoObject&lt;/code&gt; operation.&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;pre data-lang="mermaid"&gt;&lt;code&gt;sequenceDiagram
participant A as Ionic app
participant N as Native biometric plugin
participant K as Android Keystore
participant B as Mobile backend
A-&amp;gt;&amp;gt;B: Request nonce bound to enrolled device and request key
B--&amp;gt;&amp;gt;A: Short-lived one-use challenge
A-&amp;gt;&amp;gt;N: Sign challenge for mobile presence
N-&amp;gt;&amp;gt;K: Initialize authentication-bound signature
N-&amp;gt;&amp;gt;N: Show strong fingerprint prompt
K--&amp;gt;&amp;gt;N: Signature only after allowed key use
N--&amp;gt;&amp;gt;A: Signature and public metadata
A-&amp;gt;&amp;gt;B: Complete challenge
B-&amp;gt;&amp;gt;B: Verify key, purpose, nonce, expiry and current authority
B--&amp;gt;&amp;gt;A: Short-lived foreground session&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;



&lt;p&gt;Android's &lt;a href="https://developer.android.com/identity/sign-in/biometric-auth" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;biometric cryptography guide&lt;/a&gt; and &lt;a href="https://developer.android.com/privacy-and-security/keystore" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;Keystore documentation&lt;/a&gt; explain the platform primitives. Our enrollment and server authorization protocol is additional application logic.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The native policy requires strong biometric authentication for key use, uses separate aliases and domains for local testing and live mobile presence, and checks reported hardware security level. It does not collect fingerprint images or templates.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The selected app policy has no device-PIN substitute for biometric session unlock. Fresh sign-in is the recovery direction, but the current enrollment path still checks that strong biometrics are available. Do not advertise a complete biometric-unavailable recovery experience until that case is designed and tested.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


Step 3: Preserve the hardware-attestation boundary
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The phone can report that its key is backed by TEE or StrongBox and can produce a valid signature. Without verified remote attestation, the backend has not independently proved that every remote client enforces the same biometric policy.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;We therefore label server evidence as registered-device-key possession with hardware attestation &lt;strong&gt;UNVERIFIED&lt;/strong&gt;. The owner approved this explicit PoC assurance limit. A signature does not justify inventing a stronger assurance claim.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The APK contains no PF confidential-client secret, agent signing key, Graph key, Direct Line secret or Vault bootstrap credential. Its durable local state is limited to device-bound references and the consent preference. The native key stays in Android Keystore.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


Step 4: Keep first login in the system browser
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;We use backend-assisted PF login rather than embedding the provider page in the WebView. The backend owns the confidential client and provider tokens; the phone starts a device-bound transaction.&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;pre data-lang="mermaid"&gt;&lt;code&gt;sequenceDiagram
participant M as Mobile app
participant B as Backend
participant F as PF A
participant W as System browser
M-&amp;gt;&amp;gt;M: Create device key and native pending claim secret
M-&amp;gt;&amp;gt;B: Device public key and hash of claim secret
B-&amp;gt;&amp;gt;F: PAR with PKCE, state, nonce and private_key_jwt
B--&amp;gt;&amp;gt;M: Fixed-provider authorization URL
M-&amp;gt;&amp;gt;W: Open approved provider URL
W-&amp;gt;&amp;gt;F: Human sign-in
F--&amp;gt;&amp;gt;B: Code at fixed backend callback
B-&amp;gt;&amp;gt;F: Redeem code with PKCE and signed client assertion
B--&amp;gt;&amp;gt;W: One-use HTTPS App Link handoff
W-&amp;gt;&amp;gt;M: Return to verified app
M-&amp;gt;&amp;gt;B: Claim handoff with native transaction secret
B--&amp;gt;&amp;gt;M: Enrollment challenge requiring device signature&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;



&lt;p&gt;The handoff is short-lived, one-use and bound to the initiating device and claim hash. It is not a provider access token in a deep link. Process loss or missing native custody requires a fresh sign-in.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The return path is an HTTPS Android App Link. The association binds the exact hostname, package ID and APK signing certificate. A successful HTTPS GET of &lt;code&gt;assetlinks.json&lt;/code&gt; does not prove Android has verified the association on the installed phone. That is a separate device check documented in &lt;a href="https://developer.android.com/training/app-links/verify-applinks" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;Android App Link verification&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


Step 5: Separate enrollment, foreground proof and delegation
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The 30-day period is an absolute device enrollment ceiling. It does not make a PF access token valid for 30 days and does not move the original PF &lt;code&gt;auth_time&lt;/code&gt; forward.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="table-wrapper-paragraph"&gt;&lt;table&gt;
&lt;thead&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;th&gt;Object&lt;/th&gt;
&lt;th&gt;Purpose and bound&lt;/th&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;/thead&gt;
&lt;tbody&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Device enrollment&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Original verified human, device public key and absolute 30-day expiry&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Resource consent&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Separate chat/document grants, revocable and bounded by enrollment&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Foreground session&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Up to 15 minutes, replaced on fresh unlock&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Request proof&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;At most 60 seconds, one use, exact method/path/body&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Mobile authority assertion&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Profile-specific short-lived issuance under current evidence&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;PF A and PF B tokens&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Narrower audience-specific child evidence&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Provider access/refresh session&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Server-held Generic OAuth session, separate from delegated authority&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;/tbody&gt;
&lt;/table&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;p&gt;A foreground session ID alone grants no access. The app creates an ephemeral request key and signs a JWT binding session, configured audience, exact route, body hash, validity and unique &lt;code&gt;jti&lt;/code&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The server consumes replay identifiers durably and rejects a proof for access status when it is reused for chat or approval. Extra identity, scope and resource fields are not accepted in the chat body.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Current device, human, actor, organisation, grant and resource checks run again during execution. A successful fingerprint cannot override a revoked grant or suspended agent.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


Step 6: Treat resumed interaction as its own evidence type
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;We did not reuse an expired OIDC login or switch the operation to autonomous mode to bypass recent-login checks.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The mobile authority preserves the original login issuer, subject, client audience and authentication time, and records current registered-device-key presence separately. It requires the current resource grant and an independently signed registered-agent assertion before issuing delegated evidence.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The original object returned by the trusted device authority is held in an instance-private registry. JSON copies cannot be reconstructed into authority. A future cross-process handoff would need authenticated transport and replay protection, not a serialized object accepted on trust.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Real Vault/PF container verification exercised the mobile chat and document chains with their own keys and clients. The current profile uses authority/PF A/PF B maximum lifetimes of 180, 120 and 60 seconds, while enforcing remaining parent validity. This is separate from the 60-minute provider user token used for Microsoft sign-in.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


Step 7: Design foreground lifecycle as a state machine
&lt;/h2&gt;



&lt;pre data-lang="mermaid"&gt;&lt;code&gt;stateDiagram-v2
[*] --&amp;gt; Locked
Locked --&amp;gt; Starting: Sign in
Starting --&amp;gt; Browser: Fixed-provider launch
Browser --&amp;gt; Completing: Bound App Link return
Completing --&amp;gt; Consent: Manual review selected
Completing --&amp;gt; Chat: Current approval available
Consent --&amp;gt; Chat: Explicit approval
Locked --&amp;gt; Completing: Fingerprint resume
Chat --&amp;gt; Locked: Background or lock
Starting --&amp;gt; Error: Native or network failure
Completing --&amp;gt; Error: Verification failure
Chat --&amp;gt; Error: Authority or service failure
Error --&amp;gt; Starting: New explicit sign-in&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;



&lt;p&gt;Backgrounding clears the current messages, cancels owned work and discards foreground signing authority. A legitimate system-browser departure preserves only its pending native login transaction.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Generation counters prevent late callbacks, duplicate App Link events and delayed network results from opening a chat after cancellation or crossing into a new session. A failed credential-bearing operation does not automatically replay.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Every successful entry or unlock starts an empty chat. Multiple questions are supported while that foreground session is active. The app and backend do not write a durable transcript or document cache. Microsoft-hosted conversations and traces have their own retention and are not deleted merely because the app clears its screen.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


Step 8: Separate default approval from identity
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The visible default-on checkbox approves only the configured chat and document capabilities for the registered agent and existing site. It does not approve new sites, scopes or arbitrary model actions.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Turning it off requires manual resource approval. A revoked resource permission cannot be restored by a later automatic check under the same revoked binding. Unknown or unsaved preference state fails closed.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The device enrollment consent and resource delegation IDs remain different records. A phone that proves possession of its key is not automatically entitled to read documents.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


Step 9: Refresh provider credentials without creating a replay loop
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The dedicated mobile login client requires PAR, S256 PKCE and signed client authentication, with authorization code and rotating refresh grants. Provider credentials remain in CAS-protected Vault records.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Before refresh, the old refresh credential is persisted as spent. An uncertain response requires fresh sign-in. Fresh access tokens are checked for issuer, audience, subject, signature and lifetime before release to the server-side Copilot adapter.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The provider must have enough remaining validity for the foreground chat. The deployment profile requires 960 seconds before opening a 900-second conversation, keeping a margin instead of starting a session with a nearly expired token.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Compatibility of this new private-key-authenticated provider client with the already published Copilot Generic OAuth configuration remains a live gate. Sharing issuer and audience is not proof of that compatibility.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


Step 10: Prepare persistent hosting without unlimited authority
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The owner requested demos without 45-minute deployment windows or one-question limits. We introduced a separate persistent profile, preserving all spent historical allowances.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The approved standing ledger permits 100 attempted questions and 20 conversations, with additional fixed request ceilings. Counters persist across failures and restarts. This is a bounded operational allowance, not a currency meter or guaranteed enforcement of the existing $50 budget.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The private API binds only to loopback HTTPS. Exact Cloudflare routes expose the mobile API and App Link association; PF A gains only the reviewed PAR route. Workload certificate roles, durable usage, one-day audit retention and dependency supervision are separate from UI unlock.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;An owned Windows startup task is prepared to run under the existing account without a stored password or operator Vault credential. It is intentionally not installed until owner phone acceptance succeeds. Docker, unsealed Vault, the host, network, Microsoft entitlements and certificate expiry remain real availability dependencies.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


Step 11: Record deployment findings accurately
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Actual deployment exposed several mismatches that the local contracts did not catch:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;ol&gt;
&lt;li&gt;PF rejected the new client because &lt;code&gt;offline_access&lt;/code&gt; was absent from its global catalog. We obtained approval for that exact static scope addition and preserved every other setting.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;PF serialized scopes in a different order. We verified exact set equality, retained pending history and reconciled the successful write without repeating it.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;The new token manager could not publish a key ID already published by the original manager. We retained the approved signing key and disabled duplicate publication in the new manager.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;The service manifest omitted an APK certificate field. We completed metadata from the already approved certificate and APK pin while preserving the original packet.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ol&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The private runtime became ready, the five mobile clients were enabled and public configuration and association endpoints returned HTTP 200. Those facts still do not establish phone sign-in.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


Step 12: Install, distribute and diagnose on the actual phone
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The v5 candidate was installed in place using the same signing certificate. ADB inspection should target the owner's known device and must not automate fingerprint or password entry.&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight powershell"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;adb&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="w"&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;devices&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="w"&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nt"&gt;-l&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="w"&gt;
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;adb&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="w"&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nt"&gt;-s&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="w"&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="err"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;owner-device&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="err"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="w"&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;install&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="w"&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nt"&gt;-r&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="w"&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="err"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;verified-apk-path&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="err"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="w"&gt;
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;adb&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="w"&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nt"&gt;-s&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="w"&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="err"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;owner-device&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="err"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="w"&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;shell&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="w"&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;pm&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="w"&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;verify-app-links&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="w"&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nt"&gt;--re-verify&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="w"&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="err"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;package-id&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="err"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="w"&gt;
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;adb&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="w"&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nt"&gt;-s&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="w"&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="err"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;owner-device&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="err"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="w"&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;shell&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="w"&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;pm&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="w"&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;get-app-links&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="w"&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="err"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;package-id&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="err"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="w"&gt;
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;When the owner moved off-network, we added an exact, time-limited APK download route through the existing public hostname. The server serves one hash-pinned artifact, refuses other paths and query variants, and does not expose a build directory. We downloaded the public artifact and verified its hash before sharing the link.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The current reported failure is that the app stays at its sign-in button. A bounded backend initiation check returned a valid authorization destination at PF A, so the next investigation is on the native client path. We initially suspected the offline page policy, then inspected the built artifact and confirmed live mode already replaced it correctly. That suspicion was withdrawn; no unsupported fix is claimed.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;This is why the next acceptance test requires the actual phone: observe the preparing state, native key operations, pending login, browser launch and verified return without logging URLs, handoff secrets or credentials.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


Current outcome and production work
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;At the activation preparation checkpoint, 896 backend production tests, 372 simulation tests, 41 mobile tests and 12 native tests passed. Later isolated tests cover the scope amendment and APK route. These are historical checkpoint counts, not a claim that every subsequent change reran every suite.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The browser PoC has a verified document answer. Mobile core cryptography and lifecycle have local coverage, and the owner verified fingerprint behavior in the device-test build. Live mobile login, refresh, multi-turn document chat, Android association behavior and revoke/resume acceptance still need end-to-end verification.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Production work includes hardware-attestation policy, Microsoft trace protection, stronger workload isolation, rotation, reliable host recovery, billing enforcement, supported document formats and sustained availability testing. The useful result of this series is a set of explicit trust boundaries and measurable integration milestones, including the ones that remain open.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Most Next.js sites I audit look great and load fast, but Google still treats them badly. Pages sit in "Discovered, currently not indexed" for weeks, the wrong URL shows up in search, or the title Google displays is not the one you wrote.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Almost all of it comes down to a handful of things you set once in the App Router. Here is the checklist I run on every Next.js project before launch.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


1. Set metadataBase and a title template
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Without &lt;code&gt;metadataBase&lt;/code&gt;, relative URLs in canonical tags and Open Graph images can break. Set it once in the root layout, along with a title template so every page gets a consistent, unique title.&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight tsx"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="c1"&gt;// app/layout.tsx&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="k"&gt;import&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kd"&gt;type&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;Metadata&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;from&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;next&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="k"&gt;export&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kd"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;metadata&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;Metadata&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="na"&gt;metadataBase&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;new&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nc"&gt;URL&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;https://www.example.com&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;),&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="na"&gt;title&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="na"&gt;default&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;Example Studio | Web Development&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="na"&gt;template&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;%s | Example Studio&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;},&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="na"&gt;description&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;Fast websites and web apps that rank on Google.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;};&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;h2&gt;


2. Give every page its own canonical URL
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Pick one version of your domain (www or non-www, with or without a trailing slash) and make every page declare it. Duplicate URLs split your ranking signals.&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight tsx"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="c1"&gt;// app/services/page.tsx&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="k"&gt;export&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kd"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;metadata&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="na"&gt;title&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;Services&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="na"&gt;description&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;Website development, SaaS and technical SEO.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="na"&gt;alternates&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="na"&gt;canonical&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;/services/&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;},&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;};&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;Then make sure the other versions 301 redirect to it. If your canonical uses a trailing slash, set &lt;code&gt;trailingSlash: true&lt;/code&gt; in &lt;code&gt;next.config.js&lt;/code&gt; so internal links match.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


3. Generate a sitemap that includes every page you care about
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;A page that is not in your sitemap and has no internal links pointing to it is invisible. I recently saw a site where the main /services/ page was "unknown to Google" for exactly this reason.&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight typescript"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="c1"&gt;// app/sitemap.ts&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="k"&gt;import&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kd"&gt;type&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;MetadataRoute&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;from&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;next&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="k"&gt;export&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;default&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kd"&gt;function&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;sitemap&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;():&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;MetadataRoute&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;Sitemap&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="kd"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;base&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;https://www.example.com&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="kd"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;pages&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;[&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;""&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;/services/&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;/work/&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;/blog/&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;/contact/&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;];&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="k"&gt;return&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;pages&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;map&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;((&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;path&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;({&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="na"&gt;url&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="s2"&gt;`&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;${&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;base&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;}${&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;path&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;`&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="na"&gt;lastModified&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;new&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nc"&gt;Date&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(),&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;}));&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;For blog posts or case studies, pull the slugs from your CMS or database here instead of hard-coding them. Submit &lt;code&gt;/sitemap.xml&lt;/code&gt; in Google Search Console.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


4. Add robots.ts and point it at the sitemap
&lt;/h2&gt;



&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight typescript"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="c1"&gt;// app/robots.ts&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="k"&gt;import&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kd"&gt;type&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;MetadataRoute&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;from&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;next&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="k"&gt;export&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;default&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kd"&gt;function&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;robots&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;():&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;MetadataRoute&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;Robots&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="k"&gt;return&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="na"&gt;rules&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="na"&gt;userAgent&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;*&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="na"&gt;allow&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;/&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;},&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="na"&gt;sitemap&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;https://www.example.com/sitemap.xml&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;};&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;Check that staging or preview deployments are not accidentally served with &lt;code&gt;noindex&lt;/code&gt;, and that production is not accidentally blocked.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


5. Add structured data with JSON-LD
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Schema markup helps Google, and AI search tools, understand who you are and what a page is about. For a local business or freelancer, &lt;code&gt;ProfessionalService&lt;/code&gt; or &lt;code&gt;LocalBusiness&lt;/code&gt; is a good start.&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight tsx"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="kd"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;jsonLd&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;@context&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;https://schema.org&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;@type&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;ProfessionalService&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="na"&gt;name&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;Example Studio&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="na"&gt;url&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;https://www.example.com&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="na"&gt;telephone&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;+1-555-0100&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="na"&gt;areaServed&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;[&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;City A&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;City B&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;],&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;};&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="k"&gt;export&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;default&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kd"&gt;function&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;Page&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;()&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="k"&gt;return &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nt"&gt;script&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="na"&gt;type&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s"&gt;"application/ld+json"&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="na"&gt;dangerouslySetInnerHTML&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="na"&gt;__html&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;JSON&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;stringify&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;jsonLd&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;/&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;);&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;Keep the name, phone number and URL exactly the same as on your Google Business Profile and directory listings.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


6. Protect Core Web Vitals
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Use &lt;code&gt;next/image&lt;/code&gt; with explicit width and height, and add &lt;code&gt;priority&lt;/code&gt; to the hero image so LCP is not delayed.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Load fonts with &lt;code&gt;next/font&lt;/code&gt; to avoid layout shift and extra network requests.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Keep heavy client components out of the first screen. Server components by default, &lt;code&gt;"use client"&lt;/code&gt; only where you need interactivity.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Test on a real mid-range Android phone on mobile data, not just on your laptop.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


7. Fix "Discovered, currently not indexed"
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;This status means Google knows the URL but has not crawled it yet. Usually it is a priority problem, not a technical one. What helps:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Link to the page from your main navigation or from pages that are already indexed.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Make sure the page has real, unique content, not a thin template with the city name swapped.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Request indexing in Search Console URL Inspection once the above is fixed.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;p&gt;"Crawled, currently not indexed" is different: Google fetched the page and decided it was not worth indexing. That is a content quality signal, so improve the page rather than resubmitting it.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


8. Check it all in Search Console
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;After launch, inspect a few key URLs in Search Console. Confirm the Google-selected canonical matches yours, the page is mobile friendly, and the structured data is detected. Then watch the Pages report weekly for the first month.&lt;/p&gt;




&lt;p&gt;I'm Ujjwal Rupakheti, a full-stack developer and &lt;a href="https://www.ujjwalrupakheti.com.np/seo-expert-nepal/" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;SEO expert in Nepal&lt;/a&gt;. I build Next.js sites and SaaS products and run this checklist on every one. If you have questions about indexing or technical SEO on your own Next.js site, ask in the comments.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;An AI response arrives as text deltas. A Markdown renderer normally receives a document. Connecting them with render(allTextSoFar) repeatedly asks the renderer to interpret text the reader has already seen.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;I built &lt;a href="https://github.com/Lemofyz/react-stream-markdown" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;react-stream-markdown&lt;/a&gt; to explore a different boundary: keep completed blocks on screen and re-parse the unfinished suffix. The repository is currently version 0.4.1 and MIT licensed. Here is how it works, where its cost still grows, and what the published benchmark actually measures.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


Where repeated work comes from
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Suppose a response contains N characters and arrives in chunks of c characters. A full-document parser sees c characters, then 2c, then 3c, and so on. With a linear parser, the sum of characters examined is approximately N²/(2c). This models repeated parsing work; it does not mean every part of browser rendering is quadratic.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;React can reuse DOM elements after reconciliation. That does not automatically prevent an upstream Markdown parser from scanning the accumulated string. Parsing, building a tree, reconciling, layout, and painting have separate costs.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Markdown also has ambiguous intermediate states: bold delimiters and code fences may still be open. A streaming renderer needs an intermediate-display policy as well as a way to avoid revisiting stable content.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


The useful boundary is a completed block
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The renderer maintains a source offset, live DOM nodes, and the previous virtual representation of the live suffix. Each update parses state.text.slice(offset), converts its blocks to virtual nodes, and patches the live nodes.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;After patching, it advances the offset past blocks it considers finished. The implementation freezes preceding blocks when a following block has a complete first line. Frozen DOM nodes remain in the container but leave the arrays used for subsequent patch operations.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;A completed paragraph therefore stops participating in Markdown parsing and tree comparison when later paragraphs arrive. This is a finalization policy for the syntax this parser supports. It is not a universal rule that a blank line makes arbitrary Markdown immutable; document-wide dependencies would need additional invalidation rules.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Conceptually, the update is:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;ol&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Parse the accumulated text after the frozen offset.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Compare the new suffix tree with its previous tree.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Patch the live DOM nodes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Advance the offset past finalizable blocks and forget their live-state entries.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ol&gt;

&lt;p&gt;For block lengths B₁, B₂, …, repeated parsing work is closer to a sum of per-block work, roughly ΣBᵢ²/c, than repeatedly scanning the whole prefix. When blocks remain reasonably short, the parser's active working set stays small as the complete answer grows.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


Flat cost has boundaries
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;A huge paragraph, list, or open code block can keep growing without becoming finalizable. Its active suffix still gets re-parsed. Freezing does not make that case constant-time.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The component also receives cumulative text snapshots, checks whether the new text starts with the previous text, and retains the accumulated response. String construction, prefix checks, allocation, garbage collection, and browser layout sit outside the simple per-block parser model. A larger DOM may still cost more to lay out.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The defensible claim is narrower: freezing removes repeated parser and patch work on finalized blocks. It does not prove O(1) total update cost, bounded memory, or constant latency for every document.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


Patching and animation
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The active suffix is compared with its previous virtual tree. DOM APIs create or change the nodes that need updating. Raw model HTML is treated as text rather than assigned through innerHTML. Links are limited to HTTP(S) and mailto, and images appear as links.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Unfinished inline syntax is rendered optimistically: a partial bold span can already appear bold. That is an intermediate-display policy, not a guarantee that malformed Markdown will match every other parser's final interpretation.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Optional fade-in applies temporary animation spans to newly arrived characters. When the animation completes, the spans collapse into text nodes. Previously visible text does not restart its animation. Creating and animating those spans still consumes CPU time.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


What the benchmark measures
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The &lt;a href="https://github.com/Lemofyz/react-stream-markdown#benchmark-details" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;published README results&lt;/a&gt; use production builds in headless Chromium 141, three runs, and a median. The synthetic document contains 10,201 characters with lists, code, tables, and quotes. It arrives in 24-character chunks, one chunk per animation frame: 426 updates, not a recorded provider token stream.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Each renderer uses a 720-pixel-wide host. The harness synchronously applies an update and reads offsetHeight, deliberately forcing layout into that update's timing. React-based adapters use flushSync; react-stream-markdown disables its own frame batching for this test. These choices make synchronous work measurable but do not reproduce every application's scheduling behavior.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Whole-reply work is measured using the difference in Chrome's TaskDuration counter. It is not elapsed generation time, network latency, or time to first readable text. Settling is detected when text length stays unchanged for 30 frames. This is a heuristic, not proof that every animation or formatting effect has finished. The script also subtracts a fixed 3 ms from the total; that adjustment should be disclosed when reproducing the numbers.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="table-wrapper-paragraph"&gt;&lt;table&gt;
&lt;thead&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;th&gt;Renderer/configuration&lt;/th&gt;
&lt;th&gt;Published main-thread time&lt;/th&gt;
&lt;th&gt;Published slowest update&lt;/th&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;/thead&gt;
&lt;tbody&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;react-stream-markdown, fade off&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;1,100 ms&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;3.3 ms&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;react-stream-markdown, fade on&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;2,941 ms&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;7.3 ms&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Vercel Streamdown 2.7.0&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;2,031 ms&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;15.3 ms&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;@lobehub/streamdown 1.4.0, realtime&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;2,609 ms&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;14.4 ms&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;react-markdown 10.1.0 + remark-gfm 4.0.1, full string each update&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;6,384 ms&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;38.7 ms&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;/tbody&gt;
&lt;/table&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;p&gt;These are existing README results, not a fresh measurement of 0.4.1 on my current machine. The script takes medians of the metrics independently, so the displayed maximum update and total need not belong to the same run. Its slowest update is a synchronous measurement, not INP or a complete responsiveness score.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Within this workload, disabling fade-in reduces total main-thread work. Enabling it raises that total above both compared Streamdown configurations. A lower maximum synchronous update does not cancel a higher overall CPU cost.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


Making the comparison more informative
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The &lt;a href="https://github.com/Lemofyz/react-stream-markdown/tree/main/bench" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;scripts are available in the repository&lt;/a&gt;. Reproduction should record the commit, lockfile, browser version, machine, viewport, and animation settings. Test ordinary short blocks and a deliberately long single block; vary chunk size and cadence too.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The harness runs renderers in a fixed order and does not explicitly warm them up. Randomized order, more repetitions, and result distributions would help distinguish repeatable differences from noise. Correctness needs separate checks: similar rendered text lengths do not establish equivalent formatting, links, tables, or accessibility.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


Choosing a renderer
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Vercel Streamdown offers a broader rendering ecosystem, including syntax highlighting and Mermaid integrations. react-stream-markdown takes a narrower approach with no direct runtime dependencies beyond React peer dependencies. Optional math needs a renderer such as KaTeX supplied by the application, which changes the application's bundle cost.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The repository currently reports 7.8 kB gzipped for its measured JavaScript entry, with stylesheet size listed separately. That is a bundle experiment with React externalized, not the npm tarball size. Imported plugins, styles, features, and lazy chunks matter as much as the headline number.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;For a chat interface, I would choose based on required Markdown features, intermediate rendering behavior, correctness on actual responses, and profiling on target devices. This library explores how much repeated work can be removed by giving completed blocks an explicit lifetime. Its strongest result is that inspectable mechanism, rather than an unconditional claim to be the fastest renderer.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://github.com/Lemofyz/react-stream-markdown" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;Source&lt;/a&gt; · &lt;a href="https://lemofyz.github.io/react-stream-markdown/" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;Interactive demo&lt;/a&gt; · &lt;a href="https://github.com/Lemofyz/react-stream-markdown/tree/main/bench" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;Benchmark scripts&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;React’s &lt;strong&gt;Context API&lt;/strong&gt; lets you share data between components &lt;strong&gt;without passing props manually&lt;/strong&gt; through every level.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;
It’s designed for global values like theme, language, or authentication — where many components need access to the same data.&lt;/p&gt;


&lt;h2&gt;


🧩 What is React Context?
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Context provides a way to share values like &lt;code&gt;theme&lt;/code&gt;, &lt;code&gt;user&lt;/code&gt;, or &lt;code&gt;locale&lt;/code&gt; deeply in the component tree &lt;strong&gt;without prop drilling&lt;/strong&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;It helps solve this problem:&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight tsx"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="c1"&gt;// Before: prop drilling&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nc"&gt;Layout&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="na"&gt;theme&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s"&gt;"dark"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nc"&gt;Header&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="na"&gt;theme&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s"&gt;"dark"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nc"&gt;Logo&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="na"&gt;theme&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s"&gt;"dark"&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;/&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;lt;/&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nc"&gt;Header&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;lt;/&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nc"&gt;Layout&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;With Context:&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight tsx"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nc"&gt;ThemeProvider&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="na"&gt;value&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s"&gt;"dark"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nc"&gt;Layout&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;/&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;lt;/&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nc"&gt;ThemeProvider&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;






&lt;h2&gt;


⚙️ How Context Works (Under the Hood)
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;h3&gt;


Step 1 — Create
&lt;/h3&gt;



&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight tsx"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="kd"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;ThemeContext&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;React&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;createContext&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;light&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;);&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Creates a Context object with two parts:

&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A &lt;strong&gt;Provider&lt;/strong&gt; component.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A reference for the &lt;strong&gt;current value&lt;/strong&gt; inside React’s internal Fiber tree.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;h3&gt;


Step 2 — Provide
&lt;/h3&gt;



&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight tsx"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nc"&gt;ThemeContext&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nc"&gt;Provider&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="na"&gt;value&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s"&gt;"dark"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nc"&gt;App&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;/&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;lt;/&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nc"&gt;ThemeContext&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nc"&gt;Provider&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;React stores the &lt;code&gt;value&lt;/code&gt; on the Provider’s Fiber node.
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Keeps track of all &lt;strong&gt;child consumers&lt;/strong&gt; that read from this context.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;h3&gt;


Step 3 — Consume
&lt;/h3&gt;



&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight tsx"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="kd"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;theme&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;useContext&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;ThemeContext&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;);&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;React looks upward in the component tree to find the &lt;strong&gt;nearest Provider&lt;/strong&gt;.
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Returns its value.
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;If the Provider’s value changes, React &lt;strong&gt;re-renders all consumers&lt;/strong&gt; that depend on it.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;




&lt;h2&gt;


🧠 What Happens Internally
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Every Context keeps a &lt;code&gt;_currentValue&lt;/code&gt; reference on its Provider.
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;code&gt;useContext&lt;/code&gt; subscribes the component to that Provider.
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;When the Provider’s &lt;code&gt;value&lt;/code&gt; changes, React marks all consumers for re-render.
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;React compares by &lt;strong&gt;reference&lt;/strong&gt;, not by deep value.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;p&gt;So:&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight tsx"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="c1"&gt;// ❌ Causes re-renders each time&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nc"&gt;ThemeContext&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nc"&gt;Provider&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="na"&gt;value&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="na"&gt;mode&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;dark&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;...&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;lt;/&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nc"&gt;ThemeContext&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nc"&gt;Provider&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="c1"&gt;// ✅ Stable reference&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="kd"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;theme&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;useMemo&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(()&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;({&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;mode&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;}),&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;[&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;mode&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;]);&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nc"&gt;ThemeContext&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nc"&gt;Provider&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="na"&gt;value&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;theme&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;...&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;lt;/&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nc"&gt;ThemeContext&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nc"&gt;Provider&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;






&lt;h2&gt;


🧱 How to Use Context
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;h3&gt;


Create a Context + Provider
&lt;/h3&gt;



&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight tsx"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="k"&gt;import&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;createContext&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;useContext&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;useState&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;useMemo&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;from&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;react&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="kd"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;ThemeContext&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;createContext&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;();&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="k"&gt;export&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kd"&gt;function&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;ThemeProvider&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;({&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;children&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;})&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="kd"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;[&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;mode&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;setMode&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;]&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;useState&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;light&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;);&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="kd"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;value&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;useMemo&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;()&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;({&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="nx"&gt;mode&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="na"&gt;toggle&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;()&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;setMode&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;m&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;m&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;===&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;light&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;?&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;dark&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;light&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;))&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;}),&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;[&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;mode&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;]&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;);&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="k"&gt;return&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nc"&gt;ThemeContext&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nc"&gt;Provider&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="na"&gt;value&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;value&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;children&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;lt;/&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nc"&gt;ThemeContext&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nc"&gt;Provider&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="k"&gt;export&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kd"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;useTheme&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;()&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;useContext&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;ThemeContext&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;);&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;h3&gt;


Use it in Components
&lt;/h3&gt;



&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight tsx"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="kd"&gt;function&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;Header&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;()&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="kd"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;mode&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;toggle&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;useTheme&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;();&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="k"&gt;return &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nt"&gt;header&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="na"&gt;className&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;mode&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nt"&gt;button&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="na"&gt;onClick&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;toggle&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;Switch to &lt;span class="si"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;mode&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;===&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;light&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;?&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;dark&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;light&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;lt;/&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nt"&gt;button&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;lt;/&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nt"&gt;header&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;);&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;h3&gt;


Multiple Contexts
&lt;/h3&gt;



&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight tsx"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nc"&gt;AuthProvider&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nc"&gt;ThemeProvider&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nc"&gt;App&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;/&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;lt;/&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nc"&gt;ThemeProvider&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;lt;/&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nc"&gt;AuthProvider&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;






&lt;h2&gt;


🔍 When (and When Not) to Use Context
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;h3&gt;


✅ Use Context for:
&lt;/h3&gt;

&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Theme, locale, user, config&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Shared but stable global data&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;App-wide settings&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;h3&gt;


⚠️ Avoid for:
&lt;/h3&gt;

&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Rapidly changing values (inputs, lists, timers)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;High-frequency updates — causes re-renders in all consumers&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Use &lt;strong&gt;state libraries&lt;/strong&gt; (Zustand, Redux, Jotai, etc.) or &lt;strong&gt;split contexts&lt;/strong&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;




&lt;h2&gt;


🧠 How React Handles Context Internally (Fiber)
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Each Provider is a node in the &lt;strong&gt;Fiber tree&lt;/strong&gt;.
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Context changes propagate &lt;strong&gt;downward&lt;/strong&gt; through fibers.
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Each consumer using &lt;code&gt;useContext&lt;/code&gt; subscribes to that Provider.
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;On update, React traverses the subtree to re-render affected components.
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;React guarantees consistency: all consumers see the same value in one render pass.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;




&lt;h2&gt;


🚀 Optimization Tips
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;ol&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Memoize values&lt;/strong&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ol&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight tsx"&gt;&lt;code&gt;   &lt;span class="kd"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;value&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;useMemo&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(()&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;({&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;user&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;logout&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;}),&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;[&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;user&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;]);&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;ol&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Split context&lt;/strong&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ol&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight tsx"&gt;&lt;code&gt;   &lt;span class="kd"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;UserContext&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;createContext&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;();&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="kd"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;ThemeContext&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;createContext&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;();&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;→ Changing theme won’t re-render user consumers.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;ol&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Selector pattern&lt;/strong&gt;
Use libraries like &lt;code&gt;use-context-selector&lt;/code&gt; for fine-grained subscriptions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Avoid passing new objects/functions&lt;/strong&gt; each render.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ol&gt;




&lt;h2&gt;


✅ Summary
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;div class="table-wrapper-paragraph"&gt;&lt;table&gt;
&lt;thead&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;th&gt;Concept&lt;/th&gt;
&lt;th&gt;Description&lt;/th&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;/thead&gt;
&lt;tbody&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Context&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Share data deeply without prop drilling&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Provider&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Sets value for all descendants&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;&lt;strong&gt;useContext&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Reads nearest Provider’s value&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Triggers re-render&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;When &lt;code&gt;value&lt;/code&gt; prop changes by reference&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Avoid&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Rapid updates or non-memoized objects&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;/tbody&gt;
&lt;/table&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;p&gt;✨ &lt;strong&gt;React Context = global data flow with React’s rendering guarantees&lt;/strong&gt;.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;
Used right, it’s powerful and efficient — used wrong, it becomes a hidden re-render trap.&lt;/p&gt;




&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Originally published on &lt;a href="https://bitlyst.blog/p/react-context-explained" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;Bitlyst&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;React &lt;strong&gt;Fiber&lt;/strong&gt; is the internal engine that powers React’s rendering and reconciliation.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;
It’s what makes React’s updates smooth, interruptible, and concurrent.&lt;/p&gt;


&lt;h2&gt;


🧩 What is React Fiber?
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;React Fiber&lt;/strong&gt; is React’s &lt;strong&gt;reconciliation engine&lt;/strong&gt; — the system that decides &lt;em&gt;what&lt;/em&gt; needs to be rendered and &lt;em&gt;when&lt;/em&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Before React 16, React updates were &lt;strong&gt;synchronous&lt;/strong&gt; and &lt;strong&gt;blocking&lt;/strong&gt;. Once rendering started, React couldn’t pause or reprioritize work — large trees could freeze the UI.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Fiber was a complete rewrite that made React’s rendering:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;⏸ &lt;strong&gt;Interruptible&lt;/strong&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;⏱ &lt;strong&gt;Prioritized&lt;/strong&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;🔁 &lt;strong&gt;Incremental (chunked)&lt;/strong&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;💾 &lt;strong&gt;Recoverable (resumable)&lt;/strong&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;p&gt;In short: &lt;strong&gt;Fiber = React’s virtual call stack for async rendering.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;


&lt;h2&gt;


🕰️ The Old Model (Before Fiber)
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Before Fiber, React used a &lt;strong&gt;recursive&lt;/strong&gt; rendering approach — like this:&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight javascript"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="kd"&gt;function&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;renderTree&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;node&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="nx"&gt;node&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;render&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;();&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="nx"&gt;node&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;children&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;forEach&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;renderTree&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;);&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Large trees blocked the main thread.
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;The browser couldn’t respond to user input until React finished.
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;No way to pause, abort, or prioritize rendering.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;




&lt;h2&gt;


⚡ Fiber: The New Architecture
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;React Fiber breaks the rendering work into &lt;strong&gt;small units of work&lt;/strong&gt;, called &lt;strong&gt;fiber nodes&lt;/strong&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;This lets React:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Pause between chunks of work.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Resume later if the browser is busy.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Assign different priorities to updates.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Reuse previous work if nothing changed.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;p&gt;So React no longer blocks the main thread — it cooperatively yields to the browser.&lt;/p&gt;




&lt;h2&gt;


🧱 The Fiber Node Structure
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Each React component is represented by a &lt;strong&gt;Fiber node&lt;/strong&gt; — a JavaScript object with pointers and metadata.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="table-wrapper-paragraph"&gt;&lt;table&gt;
&lt;thead&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;th&gt;Field&lt;/th&gt;
&lt;th&gt;Description&lt;/th&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;/thead&gt;
&lt;tbody&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;&lt;code&gt;type&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;The component or DOM type&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;&lt;code&gt;key&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Used for list diffing&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;
&lt;code&gt;child&lt;/code&gt;, &lt;code&gt;sibling&lt;/code&gt;, &lt;code&gt;return&lt;/code&gt;
&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Pointers to other fiber nodes (linked list tree)&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;
&lt;code&gt;pendingProps&lt;/code&gt;, &lt;code&gt;memoizedProps&lt;/code&gt;, &lt;code&gt;memoizedState&lt;/code&gt;
&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Stores component state &amp;amp; props&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;&lt;code&gt;flags&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Marks what changed (update, placement, deletion)&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;&lt;code&gt;alternate&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Link to the previous fiber (for diffing old vs new trees)&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;/tbody&gt;
&lt;/table&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;p&gt;📘 Think of it as two trees:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Current tree&lt;/strong&gt; → what’s on screen.
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Work-in-progress tree&lt;/strong&gt; → what React is preparing.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;p&gt;When ready, React &lt;strong&gt;commits&lt;/strong&gt; the new tree and swaps references.&lt;/p&gt;




&lt;h2&gt;


🔁 The Two Phases of Rendering
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;h3&gt;


1️⃣ Render Phase (Reconciliation)
&lt;/h3&gt;

&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;React builds a new Fiber tree (work-in-progress).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Diffs elements vs previous render.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Calculates what to change.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Can be &lt;strong&gt;paused, aborted, or restarted&lt;/strong&gt;.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;h3&gt;


2️⃣ Commit Phase
&lt;/h3&gt;

&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;React applies all DOM mutations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Runs effects (&lt;code&gt;useEffect&lt;/code&gt;, &lt;code&gt;componentDidMount&lt;/code&gt;, etc.).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;This phase is &lt;strong&gt;synchronous&lt;/strong&gt; — React cannot pause it.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;p&gt;🧠 Render phase = “thinking”&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;
⚡ Commit phase = “doing”&lt;/p&gt;


&lt;h2&gt;


🧠 Scheduling and Priority
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Fiber works with React’s &lt;strong&gt;scheduler&lt;/strong&gt;, which assigns priority to updates:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="table-wrapper-paragraph"&gt;&lt;table&gt;
&lt;thead&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;th&gt;Priority&lt;/th&gt;
&lt;th&gt;Example&lt;/th&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;/thead&gt;
&lt;tbody&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Immediate&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;User input (typing, clicking)&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;High&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Animations&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Normal&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;State updates&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Low&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Background tasks&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Idle&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Prefetch, pre-render&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;/tbody&gt;
&lt;/table&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;p&gt;React checks between chunks:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;blockquote&gt;
&lt;p&gt;“Browser, do you have time? If not, I’ll yield and resume later.”&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/blockquote&gt;

&lt;p&gt;This is what enables &lt;strong&gt;Concurrent Rendering&lt;/strong&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;


&lt;h2&gt;


⚙️ Concurrent React (Fiber + Scheduler)
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;With &lt;strong&gt;Concurrent Mode (React 18+)&lt;/strong&gt;, Fiber can prepare multiple UI versions in parallel.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;React can:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Prepare new UI while showing the old one.
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Cancel or pause updates mid-render.
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Prioritize urgent updates (like typing).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Example:&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight tsx"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="kd"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;[&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;isPending&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;startTransition&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;]&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;useTransition&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;();&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="kd"&gt;function&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;handleInput&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;e&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="kd"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;value&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;e&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;target&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;value&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="nf"&gt;startTransition&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(()&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;setFilter&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;value&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;));&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="c1"&gt;// low priority render&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;React keeps input responsive because it renders background updates at a lower priority.&lt;/p&gt;




&lt;h2&gt;


🧬 Visualization
&lt;/h2&gt;



&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight plaintext"&gt;&lt;code&gt;      [Root Fiber]
│
┌─────┴─────┐
[App]        [Modal]
│              │
[Header]       [Button]
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;Each node is a &lt;strong&gt;Fiber&lt;/strong&gt; linked by &lt;code&gt;child&lt;/code&gt;, &lt;code&gt;sibling&lt;/code&gt;, and &lt;code&gt;return&lt;/code&gt;.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;
React walks this structure instead of the JS call stack — so it can pause or resume at any point.&lt;/p&gt;




&lt;h2&gt;


💡 Key Benefits of Fiber
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;✅ Interruptible, non-blocking rendering&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;
✅ Priority scheduling for updates&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;
✅ Recoverable rendering (pause/resume)&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;
✅ Enables Suspense, useTransition, and concurrent features&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;
✅ Better error isolation and performance profiling&lt;/p&gt;




&lt;h2&gt;


🧠 Why It Matters (Even if You Don’t Use It Directly)
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;You don’t write Fiber code yourself, but understanding it helps you reason about:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Why React sometimes delays updates.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Why “render” can happen multiple times before commit.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;How &lt;code&gt;useTransition&lt;/code&gt; and &lt;code&gt;Suspense&lt;/code&gt; work.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Why strict mode double-invokes renders (simulates concurrency).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;




&lt;h2&gt;


✅ Summary
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;div class="table-wrapper-paragraph"&gt;&lt;table&gt;
&lt;thead&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;th&gt;Concept&lt;/th&gt;
&lt;th&gt;Description&lt;/th&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;/thead&gt;
&lt;tbody&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Fiber&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;React’s internal unit of work for rendering&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Fiber Node&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Represents one component or element&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Render Phase&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Diff &amp;amp; prepare work (async, interruptible)&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Commit Phase&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Apply updates (sync)&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Scheduler&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Manages priorities of updates&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Concurrent Rendering&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Lets React multitask smoothly&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;/tbody&gt;
&lt;/table&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;p&gt;✨ &lt;strong&gt;React Fiber turned React from a recursive renderer into an asynchronous virtual machine for UI.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;
It’s the reason React 18 feels fast, smooth, and intelligent.&lt;/p&gt;




&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Originally published on &lt;a href="https://bitlyst.blog/p/react-fiber-explained" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;Bitlyst&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h1&gt;


useDeferredValue Explained
&lt;/h1&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;code&gt;useDeferredValue&lt;/code&gt; is a &lt;strong&gt;React concurrent hook&lt;/strong&gt; that lets you &lt;strong&gt;delay rendering of non-urgent values&lt;/strong&gt; so your UI stays responsive.&lt;/p&gt;




&lt;h2&gt;


🧩 What Problem Does &lt;code&gt;useDeferredValue&lt;/code&gt; Solve?
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;It helps prevent UI lag when rendering is expensive but user input must remain fast.&lt;/p&gt;




&lt;h2&gt;


⚙️ Basic Usage
&lt;/h2&gt;



&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight tsx"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="k"&gt;import&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;useDeferredValue&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;useState&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;from&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;react&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="kd"&gt;function&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;Search&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;()&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="kd"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;[&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;query&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;setQuery&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;]&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;useState&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;""&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;);&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="kd"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;deferredQuery&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;useDeferredValue&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;query&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;);&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="k"&gt;return &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;lt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nt"&gt;input&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="na"&gt;value&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;query&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="na"&gt;onChange&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;e&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;setQuery&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;e&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;target&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;value&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;/&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nc"&gt;Results&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="na"&gt;query&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;deferredQuery&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;/&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;lt;/&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;);&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;






&lt;h2&gt;


🧠 Mental Model
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;code&gt;query&lt;/code&gt; updates immediately&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;code&gt;deferredQuery&lt;/code&gt; updates when React has time&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;




&lt;h2&gt;


🔍 How It Works Under the Hood
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deferred updates are marked &lt;strong&gt;low priority&lt;/strong&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Urgent updates interrupt them&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Intermediate renders may be skipped&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;




&lt;h2&gt;


⚡ useDeferredValue vs useTransition
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;div class="table-wrapper-paragraph"&gt;&lt;table&gt;
&lt;thead&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;th&gt;Feature&lt;/th&gt;
&lt;th&gt;useDeferredValue&lt;/th&gt;
&lt;th&gt;useTransition&lt;/th&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;/thead&gt;
&lt;tbody&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Controls&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Value&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;State update&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;API&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Passive&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Active&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Pending flag&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;❌&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;✅&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;/tbody&gt;
&lt;/table&gt;&lt;/div&gt;




&lt;h2&gt;


🧱 Example: Filtering a Large List
&lt;/h2&gt;



&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight tsx"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="kd"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;deferredFilter&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;useDeferredValue&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;filter&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;);&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;






&lt;h2&gt;


⚠️ Notes
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Not a debounce&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Requires React 18+&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Delays rendering, not state&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;




&lt;h2&gt;


✅ Summary
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;code&gt;useDeferredValue&lt;/code&gt; improves UX by prioritizing urgent updates and deferring expensive rendering.&lt;/p&gt;




&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Originally published on &lt;a href="https://bitlyst.blog/p/useDeferredValue-explained" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;Bitlyst&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h1&gt;


React memo vs useMemo vs useCallback
&lt;/h1&gt;

&lt;p&gt;All three are about &lt;strong&gt;skipping unnecessary work&lt;/strong&gt;. But they work differently.&lt;/p&gt;




&lt;h2&gt;


🧠 The Core Idea
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;React re-renders a component whenever its parent re-renders — even if nothing changed. Memoization lets you say:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;blockquote&gt;
&lt;p&gt;"Only redo this if the inputs actually changed."&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/blockquote&gt;




&lt;h2&gt;


1️⃣ &lt;code&gt;React.memo&lt;/code&gt; — Skip re-rendering a component
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Wraps a &lt;strong&gt;component&lt;/strong&gt;. Skips re-render if props didn't change.&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight tsx"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="kd"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;Button&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;React&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;memo&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(({&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;onClick&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;label&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;}:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nl"&gt;onClick&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;()&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;void&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nl"&gt;label&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kr"&gt;string&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;})&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="nx"&gt;console&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;log&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;Button rendered&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;);&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="k"&gt;return&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nt"&gt;button&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="na"&gt;onClick&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;onClick&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;label&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;lt;/&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nt"&gt;button&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;});&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;Without &lt;code&gt;memo&lt;/code&gt;: Button re-renders every time the parent does.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;
With &lt;code&gt;memo&lt;/code&gt;: Button skips re-render if &lt;code&gt;onClick&lt;/code&gt; and &lt;code&gt;label&lt;/code&gt; are the same.&lt;/p&gt;


&lt;h2&gt;


2️⃣ &lt;code&gt;useMemo&lt;/code&gt; — Cache a computed value
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Memoizes the &lt;strong&gt;result&lt;/strong&gt; of an expensive calculation.&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight tsx"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="kd"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;total&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;useMemo&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(()&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="k"&gt;return&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;items&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;reduce&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;((&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;sum&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;item&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;sum&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;+&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;item&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;price&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="mi"&gt;0&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;);&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;},&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;[&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;items&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;]);&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Runs only when &lt;code&gt;items&lt;/code&gt; changes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Returns the cached value on other renders.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;p&gt;❌ Without &lt;code&gt;useMemo&lt;/code&gt;: recalculates on every render.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;
✅ With &lt;code&gt;useMemo&lt;/code&gt;: recalculates only when &lt;code&gt;items&lt;/code&gt; changes.&lt;/p&gt;


&lt;h2&gt;


3️⃣ &lt;code&gt;useCallback&lt;/code&gt; — Cache a function
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Memoizes a &lt;strong&gt;function reference&lt;/strong&gt; so it stays stable across renders.&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight tsx"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="kd"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;handleClick&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;useCallback&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(()&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="nx"&gt;console&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;log&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;clicked&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;id&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;);&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;},&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;[&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;id&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;]);&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;Without &lt;code&gt;useCallback&lt;/code&gt;, a new function is created every render — which &lt;strong&gt;breaks &lt;code&gt;React.memo&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/strong&gt; on child components.&lt;/p&gt;




&lt;h2&gt;


🔗 How They Work Together
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;code&gt;React.memo&lt;/code&gt; compares props with &lt;code&gt;===&lt;/code&gt;. Functions and objects always fail &lt;code&gt;===&lt;/code&gt; unless their reference is stable.&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight tsx"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="c1"&gt;// ❌ Button re-renders every time — new function each render&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nc"&gt;Button&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="na"&gt;onClick&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;()&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;doSomething&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;id&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="na"&gt;label&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s"&gt;"Click"&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;/&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="c1"&gt;// ✅ Button skips re-render — stable reference&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="kd"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;handleClick&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;useCallback&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(()&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;doSomething&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;id&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;),&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;[&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;id&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;]);&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nc"&gt;Button&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="na"&gt;onClick&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;handleClick&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="na"&gt;label&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s"&gt;"Click"&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;/&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;





&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight plaintext"&gt;&lt;code&gt;Parent re-renders → Props compared (===)
├─ Same reference → memo skips re-render
└─ New reference → memo re-renders child
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;






&lt;h2&gt;


⚠️ When NOT to Use Them
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Memoization has a cost — it takes memory and adds complexity. Don't use it by default.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="table-wrapper-paragraph"&gt;&lt;table&gt;
&lt;thead&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;th&gt;Situation&lt;/th&gt;
&lt;th&gt;Use memoization?&lt;/th&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;/thead&gt;
&lt;tbody&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Cheap calculation&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;❌ Not worth it&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Component renders rarely&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;❌ Skip it&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Heavy computation (&lt;code&gt;sort&lt;/code&gt;, &lt;code&gt;filter&lt;/code&gt; on large arrays)&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;✅ Yes&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Passing callbacks to memoized children&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;✅ Yes&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Passing objects/arrays as props to memoized children&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;✅ Yes&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;/tbody&gt;
&lt;/table&gt;&lt;/div&gt;




&lt;h2&gt;


🧪 Quick Example: All Three Together
&lt;/h2&gt;



&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight tsx"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="kd"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;ProductList&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;React&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;memo&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(({&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;items&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;onSelect&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;}:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;Props&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="c1"&gt;// useMemo: only recalculate when items change&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="kd"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;total&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;useMemo&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;()&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;items&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;reduce&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;((&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;s&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;i&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;s&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;+&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;i&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;price&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="mi"&gt;0&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;),&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;[&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;items&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;]&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;);&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="k"&gt;return &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nt"&gt;div&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nt"&gt;p&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;Total: $&lt;span class="si"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;total&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;lt;/&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nt"&gt;p&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="si"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;items&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;map&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;((&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;item&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nc"&gt;ProductCard&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="na"&gt;key&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;item&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;id&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="na"&gt;item&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;item&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="na"&gt;onSelect&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;onSelect&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;/&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;))&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;lt;/&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nt"&gt;div&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;);&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;});&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="kd"&gt;function&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;App&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;()&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="kd"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;[&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;cart&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;setCart&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;]&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;useState&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;([]);&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="c1"&gt;// useCallback: stable reference so ProductList doesn't re-render&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="kd"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;handleSelect&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;useCallback&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;item&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;setCart&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;((&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;prev&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;[...&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;prev&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;item&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;]),&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;[]&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;);&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="k"&gt;return&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nc"&gt;ProductList&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="na"&gt;items&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;products&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="na"&gt;onSelect&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;handleSelect&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;/&amp;gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;






&lt;h2&gt;


✅ Summary
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;div class="table-wrapper-paragraph"&gt;&lt;table&gt;
&lt;thead&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;th&gt;API&lt;/th&gt;
&lt;th&gt;Wraps&lt;/th&gt;
&lt;th&gt;Skips&lt;/th&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;/thead&gt;
&lt;tbody&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;&lt;code&gt;React.memo&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Component&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Re-render when props unchanged&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;&lt;code&gt;useMemo&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Computed value&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Recalculation when deps unchanged&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;&lt;code&gt;useCallback&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Function&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Recreation when deps unchanged&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;/tbody&gt;
&lt;/table&gt;&lt;/div&gt;




&lt;h2&gt;


✨ Final Takeaway
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;blockquote&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;code&gt;React.memo&lt;/code&gt; stops a component from re-rendering. &lt;code&gt;useMemo&lt;/code&gt; stops a value from recalculating. &lt;code&gt;useCallback&lt;/code&gt; stops a function from being recreated. Use them together — &lt;code&gt;memo&lt;/code&gt; needs &lt;code&gt;useCallback&lt;/code&gt; to actually work.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/blockquote&gt;




&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Originally published on &lt;a href="https://bitlyst.blog/p/react-memo-usememo-usecallback" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;Bitlyst&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;code&gt;useEffect&lt;/code&gt; looks simple. Add a function, add a dependency array, done.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Then production hits you with:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;a timer that logs the &lt;strong&gt;wrong count&lt;/strong&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;a fetch that sends a &lt;strong&gt;stale token&lt;/strong&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;an effect that &lt;strong&gt;runs forever&lt;/strong&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;or React Strict Mode making everything run &lt;strong&gt;twice&lt;/strong&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;p&gt;These are not random React bugs. They all come from one idea:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;blockquote&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Every render is a snapshot. Your effect remembers the values from the render that scheduled it.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/blockquote&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Once you internalize that sentence, most &lt;code&gt;useEffect&lt;/code&gt; pain disappears.&lt;/p&gt;




&lt;h2&gt;


🧠 The Core Mental Model
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;When React renders your component, it creates a &lt;strong&gt;snapshot&lt;/strong&gt; of props and state for that moment.&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight tsx"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="kd"&gt;function&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;Counter&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;()&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="kd"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;[&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;count&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;setCount&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;]&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;useState&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="mi"&gt;0&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;);&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="nf"&gt;useEffect&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(()&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="kd"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;id&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;setInterval&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(()&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="nx"&gt;console&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;log&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;count&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;);&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="c1"&gt;// 👈 frozen at the count from THIS render&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;},&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="mi"&gt;1000&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;);&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="k"&gt;return &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;()&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;clearInterval&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;id&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;);&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;},&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;[]);&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="c1"&gt;// empty deps = only first render's count&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="k"&gt;return&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nt"&gt;button&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="na"&gt;onClick&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;()&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;setCount&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;c&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;c&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;+&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="mi"&gt;1&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;count&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;lt;/&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nt"&gt;button&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;You click the button → UI shows &lt;code&gt;1&lt;/code&gt;, &lt;code&gt;2&lt;/code&gt;, &lt;code&gt;3&lt;/code&gt;…&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;
But the interval still logs &lt;code&gt;0&lt;/code&gt; forever.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Why?&lt;/strong&gt; The callback inside &lt;code&gt;setInterval&lt;/code&gt; is a &lt;strong&gt;closure&lt;/strong&gt;. It captured &lt;code&gt;count = 0&lt;/code&gt; from the first render and never saw updates.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;This is the famous &lt;strong&gt;stale closure&lt;/strong&gt; problem — the #1 &lt;code&gt;useEffect&lt;/code&gt; interview trap.&lt;/p&gt;


&lt;h2&gt;


❌ Mistake 1: Empty &lt;code&gt;[]&lt;/code&gt; When You Need Fresh Values
&lt;/h2&gt;


&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight tsx"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;useEffect&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(()&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="nf"&gt;fetch&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;`/api/user/&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;${&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;userId&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;`&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;);&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="c1"&gt;// userId from first render only&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;},&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;[]);&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;


&lt;p&gt;Looks clean. Breaks when &lt;code&gt;userId&lt;/code&gt; changes via routing or props.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;


✅ Fix
&lt;/h3&gt;


&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight tsx"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;useEffect&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(()&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="nf"&gt;fetch&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;`/api/user/&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;${&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;userId&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;`&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;);&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;},&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;[&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;userId&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;]);&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="c1"&gt;// re-run when userId changes&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;


&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Rule:&lt;/strong&gt; If your effect &lt;strong&gt;reads&lt;/strong&gt; a value from the component, that value probably belongs in the dependency array.&lt;/p&gt;


&lt;h2&gt;


❌ Mistake 2: Missing Dependencies (Ignoring ESLint)
&lt;/h2&gt;


&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight tsx"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;useEffect&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(()&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="nb"&gt;document&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;title&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="s2"&gt;`Count: &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;${&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;count&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;`&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;});&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="c1"&gt;// no deps → runs after EVERY render&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;


&lt;p&gt;Without deps, the effect runs on &lt;strong&gt;every render&lt;/strong&gt; — often causing extra work or infinite loops if the effect also sets state.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;


✅ Fix
&lt;/h3&gt;


&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight tsx"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;useEffect&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(()&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="nb"&gt;document&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;title&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="s2"&gt;`Count: &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;${&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;count&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;`&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;},&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;[&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;count&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;]);&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;


&lt;p&gt;Trust &lt;code&gt;eslint-plugin-react-hooks&lt;/code&gt;. When it says &lt;em&gt;"missing dependency"&lt;/em&gt;, it is usually right.&lt;/p&gt;


&lt;h2&gt;


❌ Mistake 3: Objects &amp;amp; Arrays in Deps → Infinite Loop
&lt;/h2&gt;


&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight tsx"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;useEffect&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(()&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="nf"&gt;loadData&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;({&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;page&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;filter&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;});&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;},&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;[{&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;page&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;filter&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;}]);&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="c1"&gt;// ❌ new object every render → effect → render → ...&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;


&lt;p&gt;In JavaScript, &lt;code&gt;{ page, filter } !== { page, filter }&lt;/code&gt;. A fresh object every render means React thinks deps &lt;strong&gt;changed&lt;/strong&gt; every time.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;


✅ Fix options
&lt;/h3&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;A) List primitives directly&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight tsx"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;useEffect&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(()&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="nf"&gt;loadData&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;({&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;page&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;filter&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;});&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;},&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;[&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;page&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;filter&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;]);&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;B) Memoize the object&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight tsx"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="kd"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;params&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;useMemo&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(()&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;({&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;page&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;filter&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;}),&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;[&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;page&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;filter&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;]);&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="nf"&gt;useEffect&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(()&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="nf"&gt;loadData&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;params&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;);&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;},&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;[&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;params&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;]);&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Rule:&lt;/strong&gt; Dependencies are compared with &lt;strong&gt;&lt;code&gt;Object.is&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/strong&gt; (like &lt;code&gt;===&lt;/code&gt;). New references every render = infinite loop.&lt;/p&gt;




&lt;h2&gt;


❌ Mistake 4: Functions in Deps Without &lt;code&gt;useCallback&lt;/code&gt;
&lt;/h2&gt;



&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight tsx"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="kd"&gt;function&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;Search&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;()&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="kd"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;[&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;q&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;setQ&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;]&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;useState&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;""&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;);&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="kd"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;search&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;()&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;fetch&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;`/api?q=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;${&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;q&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;`&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;);&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="nf"&gt;useEffect&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(()&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="nf"&gt;search&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;();&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;},&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;[&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;search&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;]);&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="c1"&gt;// search is recreated every render → loop&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;Every render creates a &lt;strong&gt;new&lt;/strong&gt; &lt;code&gt;search&lt;/code&gt; function → deps change → effect runs → state update → render → repeat.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h3&gt;


✅ Fix: define inside the effect
&lt;/h3&gt;



&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight tsx"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;useEffect&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(()&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="kd"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;search&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;()&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;fetch&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;`/api?q=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;${&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;q&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;`&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;);&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="nf"&gt;search&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;();&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;},&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;[&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;q&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;]);&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;Or wrap with &lt;code&gt;useCallback&lt;/code&gt; if the function is passed to children:&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight tsx"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="kd"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;search&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;useCallback&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(()&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="nf"&gt;fetch&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;`/api?q=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;${&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;q&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;`&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;);&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;},&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;[&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;q&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;]);&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Prefer moving logic inside the effect&lt;/strong&gt; when nothing else needs that function.&lt;/p&gt;




&lt;h2&gt;


❌ Mistake 5: Fetch Race Conditions
&lt;/h2&gt;



&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight tsx"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;useEffect&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(()&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="nf"&gt;fetch&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;`/api?q=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;${&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;query&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;`&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;then&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;r&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;r&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;json&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;())&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;then&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;setResults&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;);&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;},&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;[&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;query&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;]);&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;User types fast → request for &lt;code&gt;"a"&lt;/code&gt; finishes &lt;strong&gt;after&lt;/strong&gt; &lt;code&gt;"abc"&lt;/code&gt;. UI shows wrong data.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h3&gt;


✅ Fix: cleanup + ignore flag
&lt;/h3&gt;



&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight tsx"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;useEffect&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(()&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="kd"&gt;let&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;cancelled&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kc"&gt;false&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="nf"&gt;fetch&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;`/api?q=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;${&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;query&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;`&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;then&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;r&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;r&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;json&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;())&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;then&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;data&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="k"&gt;if &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;!&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;cancelled&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;setResults&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;data&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;);&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;});&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="k"&gt;return &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;()&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;cancelled&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kc"&gt;true&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;};&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;},&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;[&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;query&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;]);&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;Or use &lt;strong&gt;&lt;code&gt;AbortController&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/strong&gt; (see &lt;a href="https://bitlyst.blog/p/abortcontroller-practical-guide" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;AbortController guide&lt;/a&gt;).&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Rule:&lt;/strong&gt; If an effect starts async work, &lt;strong&gt;clean it up&lt;/strong&gt; on re-run or unmount.&lt;/p&gt;




&lt;h2&gt;


🔄 When You Need the Latest Value &lt;em&gt;Without&lt;/em&gt; Re-running
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Sometimes you want a stable interval/subscription but still read fresh state:&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight tsx"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="kd"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;countRef&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;useRef&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;count&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;);&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="nx"&gt;countRef&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;current&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;count&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="c1"&gt;// always latest, no extra effect runs&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="nf"&gt;useEffect&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(()&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="kd"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;id&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;setInterval&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(()&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="nx"&gt;console&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;log&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;countRef&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;current&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;);&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="c1"&gt;// ✅ always fresh&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;},&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="mi"&gt;1000&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;);&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="k"&gt;return &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;()&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;clearInterval&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;id&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;);&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;},&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;[]);&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="c1"&gt;// stable setup, fresh reads&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;Use &lt;code&gt;useRef&lt;/code&gt; when you need &lt;strong&gt;latest value&lt;/strong&gt; but don't want the effect to &lt;strong&gt;re-subscribe&lt;/strong&gt; on every change.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Related: &lt;a href="https://bitlyst.blog/p/react-useref-vs-usestate" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;useRef vs useState&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;




&lt;h2&gt;


🧪 Why Strict Mode Runs Effects Twice (Dev Only)
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;In React 18+ dev mode, Strict Mode &lt;strong&gt;mounts → unmounts → remounts&lt;/strong&gt; components to expose missing cleanups.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;You might see:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;double &lt;code&gt;fetch&lt;/code&gt; in Network tab&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;double &lt;code&gt;console.log&lt;/code&gt; on mount&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;p&gt;This is &lt;strong&gt;intentional&lt;/strong&gt;. It catches bugs like:&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight tsx"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;useEffect&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(()&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="nx"&gt;socket&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;connect&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;();&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="c1"&gt;// ❌ no cleanup → duplicate connections in prod navigations too&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;},&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;[]);&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;h3&gt;


✅ Always return cleanup
&lt;/h3&gt;



&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight tsx"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;useEffect&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(()&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="nx"&gt;socket&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;connect&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;();&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="k"&gt;return &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;()&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;socket&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;disconnect&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;();&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;},&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;[]);&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;Production does &lt;strong&gt;not&lt;/strong&gt; double-invoke. Dev pain saves prod bugs.&lt;/p&gt;




&lt;h2&gt;


🎯 Interview Cheat Sheet
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;div class="table-wrapper-paragraph"&gt;&lt;table&gt;
&lt;thead&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;th&gt;Question&lt;/th&gt;
&lt;th&gt;Short answer&lt;/th&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;/thead&gt;
&lt;tbody&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;What does &lt;code&gt;[]&lt;/code&gt; mean?&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Run once after mount (plus cleanup on unmount)&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;What if deps are omitted?&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Run after &lt;strong&gt;every&lt;/strong&gt; render&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Why stale closures?&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Effect callbacks capture values from their render snapshot&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Why infinite loops?&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Unstable deps (new object/function each render)&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;How to fix unstable deps?&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Primitives in array, &lt;code&gt;useMemo&lt;/code&gt;, &lt;code&gt;useCallback&lt;/code&gt;, or move logic inside effect&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Why double fetch in dev?&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Strict Mode remount test — add cleanup&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;
&lt;code&gt;useRef&lt;/code&gt; vs state in effects?&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Ref = read latest without re-running effect; state = triggers re-render&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;/tbody&gt;
&lt;/table&gt;&lt;/div&gt;




&lt;h2&gt;


✅ The 4 Rules to Remember
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;ol&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Every value you read inside the effect should be in deps&lt;/strong&gt; — unless you have a deliberate reason not to.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Never put freshly created objects/functions in deps&lt;/strong&gt; — use primitives, memoization, or inline them.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Always clean up&lt;/strong&gt; — timers, listeners, fetches, subscriptions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Stale closure?&lt;/strong&gt; Either add the value to deps, or store it in a &lt;code&gt;ref&lt;/code&gt; if re-running is too expensive.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ol&gt;




&lt;h2&gt;


✨ Final Takeaway
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;blockquote&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;code&gt;useEffect&lt;/code&gt; doesn't watch live variables — it remembers the snapshot from when it was scheduled.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/blockquote&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Write that on a sticky note. Next time a timer logs &lt;code&gt;0&lt;/code&gt;, a fetch sends an old token, or an effect loops forever — you'll know exactly where to look.&lt;/p&gt;




&lt;h3&gt;


Suggested follow-ups
&lt;/h3&gt;

&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;a href="https://bitlyst.blog/p/javascript-closures" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;JavaScript Closures&lt;/a&gt; — the underlying mechanism&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;a href="https://bitlyst.blog/p/react-useref-vs-usestate" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;useRef vs useState&lt;/a&gt; — when refs beat state in effects&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;a href="https://bitlyst.blog/p/abortcontroller-practical-guide" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;AbortController&lt;/a&gt; — cancel fetches on unmount&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;




&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Originally published on &lt;a href="https://bitlyst.blog/p/react-useeffect-dependencies" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;Bitlyst&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Picture a "mark as read" feature. Open a notification, and a Server Action flips it to read in the database and bumps a counter. You add a &lt;code&gt;console.log&lt;/code&gt; to the action to watch it work, open the page in &lt;code&gt;next dev&lt;/code&gt;, and the terminal prints:&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight plaintext"&gt;&lt;code&gt;[markAsRead] call #1
[markAsRead] call #2
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;One page load, two calls. Every time.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;I rebuilt that exact setup on this blog's codebase (Next.js 16.4, React 19) as a ten-line test page, and got the same thing: two &lt;code&gt;POST&lt;/code&gt; requests with the same &lt;code&gt;next-action&lt;/code&gt; id in the network tab, two log lines on the server.&lt;/p&gt;




&lt;h2&gt;


The wrong turn: blaming Next.js
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Two calls from one load looks like a framework bug. Maybe Next.js retries actions. Maybe the page renders twice on the server and each render fires the action. Maybe HMR left an old copy of the component mounted.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;None of those hold up. Here's the whole client component:&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight tsx"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;use client&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="k"&gt;import&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;useEffect&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;from&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;react&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="k"&gt;import&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;markAsRead&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;from&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;./actions&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="k"&gt;export&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kd"&gt;function&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;Notification&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;({&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;id&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;}:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nl"&gt;id&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kr"&gt;string&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;})&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="nf"&gt;useEffect&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(()&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="nf"&gt;markAsRead&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;id&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;);&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;},&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;[&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;id&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;]);&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="k"&gt;return&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nt"&gt;p&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;…&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;lt;/&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nt"&gt;p&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;Server Actions never run during rendering. They run when the browser calls them, and the only thing calling this one is &lt;code&gt;useEffect&lt;/code&gt;. So the real question is: why does the effect run twice?&lt;/p&gt;




&lt;h2&gt;


The reveal: React mounts everything twice in development
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Next.js turns on React &lt;strong&gt;Strict Mode&lt;/strong&gt; by default in the App Router (the &lt;code&gt;reactStrictMode&lt;/code&gt; docs say so: it's been &lt;code&gt;true&lt;/code&gt; by default since Next.js 13.5.1). In development, Strict Mode deliberately stress-tests every component when it first appears:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What Strict Mode does with your effect in development&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight plaintext"&gt;&lt;code&gt;1. Mount              — The component appears on the page
2. Run effect         — useEffect fires: first call to markAsRead
3. Simulated unmount  — React pretends the component left the page
4. Run cleanup        — Your cleanup function runs, if you returned one
5. Mount again        — React puts it back, keeping the same state
6. Run effect again   — useEffect fires again: second call to markAsRead
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;In production the middle steps don't exist, so the effect runs once.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;That's why it only happens on localhost. In a production build there's no simulated remount. I checked this on a production build of the blog too: its view counter, which posts from a &lt;code&gt;useEffect&lt;/code&gt;, sent one &lt;code&gt;POST&lt;/code&gt; under &lt;code&gt;next start&lt;/code&gt; and two under &lt;code&gt;next dev&lt;/code&gt; (the first one cancelled by its cleanup).&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;React does this on purpose. A real user can make a component unmount and mount again: navigate away and back, or a parent that hides and shows it. Strict Mode makes that happen immediately, so you find out now whether your effect survives it.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;blockquote&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Strict Mode isn't calling your action twice. It's showing you that your code would call it twice if the component ever remounted.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/blockquote&gt;




&lt;h2&gt;


The fix: decide what the call is for
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;There are two kinds of "call an action when this shows up," and they get different fixes.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;It's caused by something the user did.&lt;/strong&gt; Marking as read, liking, saving, buying. These belong in an event handler or a form, not an effect. The click is the cause, so the click should make the call:&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight tsx"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="c1"&gt;// before: fires whenever the component mounts&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="nf"&gt;useEffect&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(()&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="nf"&gt;markAsRead&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;id&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;);&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;},&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;[&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;id&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;]);&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="c1"&gt;// after: fires once per click&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nt"&gt;button&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="na"&gt;onClick&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;()&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;markAsRead&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;id&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;Open&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;lt;/&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nt"&gt;button&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="c1"&gt;// or with a form, which also works before JavaScript loads&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nt"&gt;form&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="na"&gt;action&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;markAsRead&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;bind&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="kc"&gt;null&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;id&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nt"&gt;button&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;Open&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;lt;/&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nt"&gt;button&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;lt;/&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nt"&gt;form&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;It's caused by the component being shown.&lt;/strong&gt; Page views and analytics are the classic case. Here the effect is the right place, so make the server safe to call twice. This blog's view counter does exactly that: the &lt;code&gt;POST&lt;/code&gt; handler counts one read per visitor per post per day, so a second request changes nothing.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;There's also the trick you'll find on Stack Overflow, a ref that remembers it already ran:&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight tsx"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="kd"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;ran&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;useRef&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="kc"&gt;false&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;);&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="nf"&gt;useEffect&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(()&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="k"&gt;if &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;ran&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;current&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;return&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="nx"&gt;ran&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;current&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kc"&gt;true&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="nf"&gt;markAsRead&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;id&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;);&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;},&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;[&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;id&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;]);&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;It works: my test page logged one call with it instead of two. But the React docs advise against it, because it silences the warning without fixing the cause. The day the component really remounts, the ref starts over at &lt;code&gt;false&lt;/code&gt; and you get a second call in production anyway.&lt;/p&gt;




&lt;h2&gt;


The rule
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;If an action changes data because of something the user did, call it from the event that caused it. If it has to run from an effect, make the server handle it arriving twice.&lt;/p&gt;




&lt;h2&gt;


TL;DR
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Next.js enables React Strict Mode by default in the App Router, and in development Strict Mode mounts, unmounts and remounts every component.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;So a Server Action called from &lt;code&gt;useEffect&lt;/code&gt; runs twice in &lt;code&gt;next dev&lt;/code&gt; and once in production.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;In a test page on this blog, the action logged two calls in dev; a production build of the view counter sent one request.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Move user-caused mutations (read, like, save) into event handlers or &lt;code&gt;&amp;lt;form action&amp;gt;&lt;/code&gt;.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;For effects that must call the server, like view tracking, make the endpoint idempotent instead of hiding the second call with a ref.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;




&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Originally published on &lt;a href="https://bitlyst.blog/p/nextjs-server-action-runs-twice-dev" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;Bitlyst&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h1&gt;


useTransition Explained
&lt;/h1&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;code&gt;useTransition&lt;/code&gt; is a React 18+ &lt;strong&gt;concurrent hook&lt;/strong&gt; that lets you mark some state updates as &lt;strong&gt;non-urgent&lt;/strong&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;This helps your app stay responsive by making React prioritize:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;✅ urgent updates (typing, clicking, input responsiveness)
over&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;⏳ slow UI updates (big list rendering, expensive filtering, heavy page transitions)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;




&lt;h2&gt;


🧩 The Problem It Solves
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Imagine a search input where filtering is heavy:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;User types: input updates&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;At the same time, you render a huge list based on the text&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Without &lt;code&gt;useTransition&lt;/code&gt;, React treats both as equally urgent → typing can feel laggy.&lt;/p&gt;




&lt;h2&gt;


⚙️ Basic API
&lt;/h2&gt;



&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight tsx"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="k"&gt;import&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;useTransition&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;useState&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;from&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;react&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="k"&gt;export&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;default&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kd"&gt;function&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;SearchPage&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;({&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;items&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;}:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nl"&gt;items&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kr"&gt;string&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;[]&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;})&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="kd"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;[&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;query&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;setQuery&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;]&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;useState&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;""&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;);&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="kd"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;[&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;filter&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;setFilter&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;]&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;useState&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;""&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;);&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="kd"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;[&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;isPending&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;startTransition&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;]&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;useTransition&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;();&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="kd"&gt;function&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;onChange&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;e&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;React&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;ChangeEvent&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;HTMLInputElement&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="kd"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;value&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;e&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;target&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;value&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="c1"&gt;// ✅ urgent: update input right away&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="nf"&gt;setQuery&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;value&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;);&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="c1"&gt;// ⏳ non-urgent: update expensive list/filter&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="nf"&gt;startTransition&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(()&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="nf"&gt;setFilter&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;value&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;);&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;});&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="kd"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;filtered&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;items&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;filter&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;((&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;x&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;x&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;includes&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;filter&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;));&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="k"&gt;return &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nt"&gt;div&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nt"&gt;input&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="na"&gt;value&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;query&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="na"&gt;onChange&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;onChange&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;/&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="si"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;isPending&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;amp;&amp;amp;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nt"&gt;p&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;Updating results…&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;lt;/&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nt"&gt;p&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nt"&gt;ul&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="si"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;filtered&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;map&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;((&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;x&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nt"&gt;li&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="na"&gt;key&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;x&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;x&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;lt;/&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nt"&gt;li&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;))&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;lt;/&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nt"&gt;ul&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;lt;/&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nt"&gt;div&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;);&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;h3&gt;


What you get
&lt;/h3&gt;

&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;code&gt;startTransition(fn)&lt;/code&gt; marks updates inside as &lt;strong&gt;transition&lt;/strong&gt; (low priority).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;code&gt;isPending&lt;/code&gt; becomes &lt;code&gt;true&lt;/code&gt; while React is working on those updates.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;




&lt;h2&gt;


🧠 Mental Model
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Think of React updates like a queue with priorities:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Urgent lane&lt;/strong&gt;: typing, clicks, pointer movement&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Transition lane&lt;/strong&gt;: slow rendering that can wait&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;code&gt;startTransition&lt;/code&gt; moves updates into the &lt;strong&gt;transition lane&lt;/strong&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;So the user experience becomes:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;input stays snappy ✅&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;expensive rendering happens a bit later ⏳&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;




&lt;h2&gt;


🔍 How It Works Under the Hood
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;React Fiber + Scheduler does this:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;ol&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;code&gt;setQuery(value)&lt;/code&gt; schedules an &lt;strong&gt;urgent update&lt;/strong&gt;.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;code&gt;startTransition(() =&amp;gt; setFilter(value))&lt;/code&gt; schedules a &lt;strong&gt;low priority update&lt;/strong&gt;.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;If the user keeps typing, React may:

&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;pause the low priority render&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;restart it with the latest value&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;skip intermediate renders&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ol&gt;

&lt;p&gt;That’s why transitions feel smooth: React avoids wasting work.&lt;/p&gt;




&lt;h2&gt;


⚡ useTransition vs useDeferredValue
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;div class="table-wrapper-paragraph"&gt;&lt;table&gt;
&lt;thead&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;th&gt;Feature&lt;/th&gt;
&lt;th&gt;useTransition&lt;/th&gt;
&lt;th&gt;useDeferredValue&lt;/th&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;/thead&gt;
&lt;tbody&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;You control&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;a state update&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;a derived value&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;API style&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Active (&lt;code&gt;startTransition&lt;/code&gt;)&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Passive (&lt;code&gt;useDeferredValue(value)&lt;/code&gt;)&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Pending indicator&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;✅ &lt;code&gt;isPending&lt;/code&gt;
&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;❌ no built-in pending&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Best for&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;triggering work&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;delaying derived rendering&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Typical use&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;page transitions, filtering&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;search input results, previews&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;/tbody&gt;
&lt;/table&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Rule of thumb&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Use &lt;strong&gt;useTransition&lt;/strong&gt; when you want to say: “this update can wait.”&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Use &lt;strong&gt;useDeferredValue&lt;/strong&gt; when you want: “render using an older value until you have time.”&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;




&lt;h2&gt;


✅ Great Use Cases
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Filtering large lists&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Switching tabs with heavy content&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Updating charts&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Navigating to a route that triggers lots of work&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Anything where “loading/pending” UX helps&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;




&lt;h2&gt;


⚠️ What useTransition is NOT
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;❌ It is &lt;strong&gt;not&lt;/strong&gt; debounce/throttle&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;❌ It does &lt;strong&gt;not&lt;/strong&gt; run work in a separate thread&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;❌ It doesn’t magically make slow code fast — it just makes the UI stay responsive&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;p&gt;If your render is extremely slow, consider:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;memoization (&lt;code&gt;useMemo&lt;/code&gt;, &lt;code&gt;React.memo&lt;/code&gt;)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;virtualization (react-window)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;splitting components / code-splitting&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;improving algorithms&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;




&lt;h2&gt;


🧱 Common Mistakes
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;h3&gt;


1) Putting urgent updates inside transition
&lt;/h3&gt;



&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight tsx"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;startTransition&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(()&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="nf"&gt;setQuery&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;value&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;);&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="c1"&gt;// ❌ makes typing laggy&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;});&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;Keep input updates urgent.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h3&gt;


2) Creating new heavy objects on every render
&lt;/h3&gt;

&lt;p&gt;If your filtered list is recomputed every render, also consider memoizing or pre-indexing.&lt;/p&gt;




&lt;h2&gt;


🔁 &lt;code&gt;isPending&lt;/code&gt; UX pattern
&lt;/h2&gt;



&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight tsx"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;isPending&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;?&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nc"&gt;Spinner&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;/&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nc"&gt;Results&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;/&amp;gt;}&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;or keep results visible and show subtle hint:&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight tsx"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;isPending&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;amp;&amp;amp;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nt"&gt;small&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;Updating…&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;lt;/&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nt"&gt;small&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;gt;}&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;






&lt;h2&gt;


✅ Summary
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;code&gt;useTransition&lt;/code&gt; marks updates as &lt;strong&gt;low priority&lt;/strong&gt;.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;It protects user input from being blocked by heavy renders.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Powered by &lt;strong&gt;Fiber + Scheduler&lt;/strong&gt;, React can pause/restart work.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Pair it with good performance practices for best results.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;p&gt;✨ &lt;strong&gt;useTransition makes React apps feel instant by keeping “urgent UI” always responsive.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;




&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Originally published on &lt;a href="https://bitlyst.blog/p/useTransition-explained" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;Bitlyst&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://media2.dev.to/dynamic/image/width=800%2Cheight=%2Cfit=scale-down%2Cgravity=auto%2Cformat=auto/https%3A%2F%2Fdev-to-uploads.s3.us-east-2.amazonaws.com%2Fuploads%2Farticles%2Fwhd3tzlb57cfx8cnm38w.png" class="article-body-image-wrapper"&gt;&lt;img src="https://media2.dev.to/dynamic/image/width=800%2Cheight=%2Cfit=scale-down%2Cgravity=auto%2Cformat=auto/https%3A%2F%2Fdev-to-uploads.s3.us-east-2.amazonaws.com%2Fuploads%2Farticles%2Fwhd3tzlb57cfx8cnm38w.png" alt=" " width="800" height="533"&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;How to build AI agents that survive failures, resume interrupted tasks, handle approvals, and execute reliably in production.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


1. Why Do AI Agents Need Durable Execution?
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Most AI applications start with a relatively straightforward execution model.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;A user sends a message, the application invokes an LLM, the model may call a tool, and the application returns a response.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;For simple interactions, this is usually sufficient.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;However, agentic applications introduce a different level of complexity.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;An agent may execute several model calls, invoke multiple tools, delegate tasks to other agents, wait for external systems, and require human approval before continuing.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Consider an agent responsible for reviewing and processing a business request:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;ol&gt;
&lt;li&gt;The user submits a request.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;The agent analyzes the request.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;It retrieves information from internal systems.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;It delegates an analysis task to a specialist agent.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;It generates a proposed action.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;It requests approval from an authorized user.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;After approval, it executes the operation.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;It records the result and completes the task.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ol&gt;

&lt;p&gt;This workflow may take seconds, minutes, or even several hours.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Now imagine the application crashes after step five.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;What happens to the work already completed?&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Does the agent start over? Are previous model calls executed again? Will the user need to submit the request again? Could an external operation be executed twice?&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;These are not unusual edge cases. They are fundamental engineering problems in long-running AI systems.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;A conventional in-memory agent generally keeps its execution state inside the current process. When that process terminates unexpectedly, the state may be lost.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Saving conversation messages to a database does not solve this problem by itself.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Durable Execution is the ability to preserve workflow progress and resume execution from a known point after failures, interruptions, or external events.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;It allows us to build agents that are not dependent on one uninterrupted application process.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The objective is not merely to make an agent remember what happened. It is to make the entire execution reliable.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


2. State Persistence vs. Durable Execution
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;These concepts are related, but they are not interchangeable.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h3&gt;


State Persistence
&lt;/h3&gt;

&lt;p&gt;State persistence means storing information so that it can be retrieved later.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;For an AI application, this might include:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Conversation history&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;User preferences&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Current task status&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Agent configuration&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Intermediate results&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Retrieved documents&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Tool execution results&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;p&gt;For example, we can store conversation messages in PostgreSQL and load them when a user returns to the application.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;This provides conversation continuity.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;However, storing messages does not automatically tell us where an interrupted workflow should resume.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h3&gt;


Durable Execution
&lt;/h3&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Durable execution goes further.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;It records the execution progress and the results of completed steps so that the workflow can continue without repeating all previous work.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Consider this example:&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight plaintext"&gt;&lt;code&gt;Agent Workflow
|
v
Retrieve Context
|
v
LLM Analysis
|
v
Execute Tool
|
v
Generate Report
|
X Application Crashes
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;Without durable execution, the application may need to restart the entire workflow.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;With checkpointing:&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight plaintext"&gt;&lt;code&gt;Agent Workflow
|
v
Retrieve Context       ✓ Checkpoint
|
v
LLM Analysis           ✓ Checkpoint
|
v
Execute Tool           ✓ Checkpoint
|
v
Generate Report        X Failed
|
v
Application Restarts
|
v
Resume from last
completed checkpoint
|
v
Generate Report
|
v
Complete
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;The completed results can be reused while the failed operation is retried.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;This distinction becomes particularly important when model calls are expensive or when tools perform operations against external systems.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h3&gt;


What about Agent Memory?
&lt;/h3&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Memory and durable execution are also different concepts.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="table-wrapper-paragraph"&gt;&lt;table&gt;
&lt;thead&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;th&gt;Concept&lt;/th&gt;
&lt;th&gt;Responsibility&lt;/th&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;/thead&gt;
&lt;tbody&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Conversation history&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;What the user and agent discussed&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Short-term memory&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Information needed during the current interaction&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Long-term memory&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Information retained across interactions&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Checkpointing&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Where execution stopped and what has completed&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Durable execution&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;How the workflow resumes and continues reliably&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;/tbody&gt;
&lt;/table&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;p&gt;For example, an agent may remember a user's preferences through long-term memory while a durable workflow maintains the execution state of an ongoing approval process.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;One does not replace the other.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Reference:&lt;/strong&gt; &lt;a href="https://docs.langchain.com/oss/javascript/langgraph/persistence" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;LangGraph — Persistence&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


3. Core Concepts Behind Durable Execution
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Before choosing a framework, it helps to understand the underlying engineering primitives.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h3&gt;


3.1. Checkpointing
&lt;/h3&gt;

&lt;p&gt;A checkpoint is a persisted representation of workflow state at a specific point in execution.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Depending on the runtime, it may include:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Completed step identifiers&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Step outputs&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Workflow state&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Execution metadata&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Pending operations&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Current task status&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;References to external payloads&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;p&gt;When a workflow resumes, the runtime uses these checkpoints to determine which operations have already completed.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Checkpointing is particularly useful when a workflow contains expensive or long-running operations.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;However, we should avoid storing unnecessarily large objects in every checkpoint.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;For example, instead of persisting a 50 MB document inside workflow state, we can store it in object storage and keep only its identifier and metadata in the checkpoint.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h3&gt;


3.2. Replay
&lt;/h3&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Replay is the process of reconstructing workflow execution using its previously recorded history.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Some durable execution engines replay workflow code to rebuild the current execution state.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;This introduces an important engineering requirement: deterministic execution.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;If the same workflow is replayed with the same history, it should make the same workflow decisions.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Consider:&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight typescript"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="k"&gt;async&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kd"&gt;function&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;workflow&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;()&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="kd"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;timestamp&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nb"&gt;Date&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;now&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;();&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="c1"&gt;// Continue execution...&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;If the workflow is replayed later, &lt;code&gt;Date.now()&lt;/code&gt; returns a different value.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;This could change its execution path.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Likewise, direct network calls, random values, and database queries should not be performed inside deterministic workflow definitions when the runtime expects replay-safe code.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;These operations should be isolated into activities or durable steps.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;For example:&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight typescript"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="k"&gt;async&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kd"&gt;function&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;workflow&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;()&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="kd"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;timestamp&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;await&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;getCurrentTimeStep&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;();&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="c1"&gt;// Continue using the recorded result...&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;The durable runtime records the step result and reuses it during replay.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;This is a foundational concept in systems such as Temporal.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h3&gt;


3.3. Durable Steps
&lt;/h3&gt;

&lt;p&gt;A durable workflow is usually divided into independent execution units.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;For example:&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight plaintext"&gt;&lt;code&gt;Workflow
|
+-- Step 1: Retrieve documents
|
+-- Step 2: Generate analysis
|
+-- Step 3: Validate output
|
+-- Step 4: Request approval
|
+-- Step 5: Execute operation
|
+-- Step 6: Save final result
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;Each completed step produces a checkpoint.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;If step five fails, the workflow should not need to repeat document retrieval, model analysis, and validation.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;This also allows us to apply different retry policies to different operations.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h3&gt;


3.4. Durable Waits
&lt;/h3&gt;

&lt;p&gt;A workflow may need to wait for something that is outside the application's control.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Examples include:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Human approval&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;An external webhook&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A scheduled execution time&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A payment confirmation&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A response from another agent&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Completion of a long-running background operation&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;p&gt;A regular asynchronous function can wait for an event, but keeping the process alive indefinitely is not a scalable approach.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Durable execution systems can suspend the workflow, persist its state, and resume it when the expected event arrives.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The application does not need to keep a worker occupied during the waiting period.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h3&gt;


3.5. Retries and Recovery
&lt;/h3&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Failures should be handled according to their type.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;A network timeout, provider rate limit, validation error, and authorization failure should not necessarily follow the same retry policy.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;A retry policy should define:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Maximum attempts&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Initial delay&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Backoff strategy&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Maximum delay&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Retryable error categories&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Overall execution deadline&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Cancellation behavior&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;p&gt;A durable execution engine provides the infrastructure for retries, but the application still needs to define what should be retried and why.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


4. The Most Important Concept: Idempotency
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;This is one of the most important aspects of building reliable AI agents.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Durable execution can resume workflows and retry failed steps. But retries can introduce duplicate side effects.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Consider an agent that generates a report and publishes it to an external system.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The operation succeeds, but the application crashes before the workflow records the result.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;When execution resumes, the workflow may attempt to publish the report again.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Without additional protection, we could create two reports.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;This is why idempotency matters.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;An operation is idempotent when executing it multiple times with the same logical input produces the same intended outcome as executing it once.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;For example, consider a report publishing API:&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight typescript"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="k"&gt;async&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kd"&gt;function&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;publishReport&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;input&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="nl"&gt;reportId&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kr"&gt;string&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="nl"&gt;content&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kr"&gt;string&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="nl"&gt;operationId&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kr"&gt;string&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;})&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="kd"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;response&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;await&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;fetch&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s1"&gt;https://api.example.com/reports&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="na"&gt;method&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s1"&gt;POST&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="na"&gt;headers&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s1"&gt;Content-Type&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s1"&gt;application/json&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s1"&gt;Idempotency-Key&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;input&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;operationId&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;},&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="na"&gt;body&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;JSON&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;stringify&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;({&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="na"&gt;reportId&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;input&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;reportId&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="na"&gt;content&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;input&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;content&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;}),&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;},&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;);&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="k"&gt;if &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;!&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;response&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;ok&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="k"&gt;throw&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;new&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nc"&gt;Error&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="s2"&gt;`Report publishing failed: &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;${&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;response&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;status&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;`&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;);&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="k"&gt;return&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;response&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;json&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;();&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;The important detail is &lt;code&gt;operationId&lt;/code&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;It must be generated and persisted by a trusted part of the application before the external operation is attempted. It should not be an arbitrary identifier generated by the LLM.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The receiving service must also implement idempotency-key handling. Merely sending the header does not guarantee duplicate prevention.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h3&gt;


Why isn't exactly-once execution automatic?
&lt;/h3&gt;

&lt;p&gt;This is a common misunderstanding.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;A workflow engine can guarantee that a successfully checkpointed step is not unnecessarily executed again during replay.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;However, an external side effect and the workflow's checkpoint cannot always participate in the same atomic transaction.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;There is a failure window:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;ol&gt;
&lt;li&gt;An external API accepts the request.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;The external operation succeeds.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;The application crashes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;The workflow has not recorded the successful result.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;The workflow retries.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ol&gt;

&lt;p&gt;This means we should not assume that every external operation executes exactly once.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;A more accurate approach is to design for:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;At-least-once execution attempts.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Idempotent external operations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Durable operation identifiers.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deduplication at the receiving service.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Transactional outbox patterns where appropriate.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Reconciliation for operations whose result is uncertain.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;p&gt;For critical business operations, this distinction is non-negotiable.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;A durable workflow is not a substitute for transactional business design.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


5. Human-in-the-Loop: When an Agent Needs Approval
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Not every operation should be executed automatically.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;In enterprise applications, an agent may need authorization before performing an operation that has financial, operational, or security implications.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;For example:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Publishing a report&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Updating customer information&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Executing a database modification&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Approving a business transaction&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Changing production configuration&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Triggering an external workflow&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;p&gt;A traditional implementation may look like this:&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight plaintext"&gt;&lt;code&gt;Agent
|
v
Generate Proposed Action
|
v
Save Pending Approval
|
v
Notify User
|
v
Wait for Response
|
v
User Approves
|
v
Continue Agent
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;The problem is that the application needs to preserve enough state to resume the original execution.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;A durable workflow makes this much easier.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;It can:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;ol&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Execute the agent until an approval boundary.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Persist the current state.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Suspend execution.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Notify the appropriate user.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Wait for an approval event.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Resume from the saved state.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Continue or abort based on the decision.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ol&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The approval process may take seconds, hours, or days.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Importantly, the application should verify the identity and authorization of the person responding. The decision should be bound to the original operation, its parameters, and its expiration policy.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;An approval should not be a generic boolean that can be reused for another action.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


6. Implementing Durable Agents with Vercel AI SDK
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;For TypeScript-based applications, the Vercel AI SDK ecosystem provides an interesting integration through &lt;code&gt;WorkflowAgent&lt;/code&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The standard &lt;code&gt;ToolLoopAgent&lt;/code&gt; runs its execution loop in memory.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;This is suitable for short interactions, but its progress can be lost when the underlying process terminates.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;code&gt;WorkflowAgent&lt;/code&gt;, provided through &lt;code&gt;@ai-sdk/workflow&lt;/code&gt;, runs the agent inside the Vercel Workflow runtime.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;It provides:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Persistent execution progress&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Independent tool retries&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Recovery after process interruptions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Human approval that can survive long waits&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Workflow-level execution visibility&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Resumable chat streaming through &lt;code&gt;WorkflowChatTransport&lt;/code&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;p&gt;An important distinction: durability comes from the Workflow runtime, not simply from changing the agent class.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h3&gt;


Step 1: Install the packages
&lt;/h3&gt;



&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight shell"&gt;&lt;code&gt;pnpm add ai @ai-sdk/workflow workflow zod
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;h3&gt;


Step 2: Define durable tool operations
&lt;/h3&gt;

&lt;p&gt;A tool operation can be marked as a durable step using the &lt;code&gt;'use step'&lt;/code&gt; directive.&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight typescript"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="k"&gt;async&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kd"&gt;function&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;searchDocumentsStep&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;input&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="nl"&gt;query&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kr"&gt;string&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;})&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s1"&gt;use step&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="kd"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;response&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;await&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;fetch&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="s2"&gt;`https://api.example.com/search?q=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;${&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;encodeURIComponent&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="nx"&gt;input&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;query&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;)}&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;`&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;);&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="k"&gt;if &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;!&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;response&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;ok&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="k"&gt;throw&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;new&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nc"&gt;Error&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="s2"&gt;`Document search failed: &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;${&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;response&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;status&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;`&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;);&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="k"&gt;return&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;response&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;json&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;();&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;The runtime can persist the result of this step and retry it independently when a retryable failure occurs.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;This is particularly useful when the operation interacts with an unreliable external service.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h3&gt;


Step 3: Create a WorkflowAgent
&lt;/h3&gt;



&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight typescript"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="k"&gt;import&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="nx"&gt;WorkflowAgent&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="kd"&gt;type&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;ModelCallStreamPart&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;from&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s1"&gt;@ai-sdk/workflow&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="k"&gt;import&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="nx"&gt;convertToModelMessages&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="nx"&gt;tool&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="kd"&gt;type&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;UIMessage&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;from&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s1"&gt;ai&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="k"&gt;import&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;getWritable&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;from&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s1"&gt;workflow&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="k"&gt;import&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;z&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;from&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s1"&gt;zod&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="k"&gt;async&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kd"&gt;function&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;searchDocumentsStep&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;input&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="nl"&gt;query&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kr"&gt;string&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;})&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s1"&gt;use step&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="kd"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;response&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;await&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;fetch&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="s2"&gt;`https://api.example.com/search?q=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;${&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;encodeURIComponent&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="nx"&gt;input&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;query&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;)}&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;`&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;);&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="k"&gt;if &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;!&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;response&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;ok&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="k"&gt;throw&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;new&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nc"&gt;Error&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s1"&gt;Document search failed&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;);&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="k"&gt;return&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;response&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;json&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;();&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="k"&gt;async&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kd"&gt;function&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;publishReportStep&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;input&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="nl"&gt;reportId&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kr"&gt;string&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;})&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s1"&gt;use step&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="kd"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;response&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;await&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;fetch&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s1"&gt;https://api.example.com/reports/publish&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="na"&gt;method&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s1"&gt;POST&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="na"&gt;headers&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s1"&gt;Content-Type&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s1"&gt;application/json&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;},&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="na"&gt;body&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;JSON&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;stringify&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;input&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;),&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;},&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;);&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="k"&gt;if &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;!&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;response&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;ok&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="k"&gt;throw&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;new&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nc"&gt;Error&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s1"&gt;Report publishing failed&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;);&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="k"&gt;return&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;response&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;json&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;();&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="k"&gt;export&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;async&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kd"&gt;function&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;runAssistant&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="nx"&gt;messages&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;UIMessage&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;[],&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s1"&gt;use workflow&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="kd"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;agent&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;new&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nc"&gt;WorkflowAgent&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;({&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="na"&gt;model&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s1"&gt;anthropic/claude-sonnet-4-6&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="na"&gt;instructions&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="s2"&gt;`
You are an enterprise research assistant.

Search internal documentation when needed.
Prepare reports based on verified information.
Never publish a report without approval.
`&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="na"&gt;tools&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="na"&gt;searchDocuments&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;tool&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;({&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="na"&gt;description&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s1"&gt;Search internal documentation.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="na"&gt;inputSchema&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;z&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;object&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;({&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="na"&gt;query&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;z&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;string&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(),&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;}),&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="na"&gt;execute&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;searchDocumentsStep&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;}),&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="na"&gt;publishReport&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;tool&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;({&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="na"&gt;description&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s1"&gt;Publish a prepared report.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="na"&gt;inputSchema&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;z&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;object&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;({&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="na"&gt;reportId&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;z&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;string&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(),&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;}),&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="na"&gt;needsApproval&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kc"&gt;true&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="na"&gt;execute&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;publishReportStep&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;}),&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;},&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;});&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="kd"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;result&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;await&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;agent&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;stream&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;({&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="na"&gt;messages&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;convertToModelMessages&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;messages&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;),&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="na"&gt;writable&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;getWritable&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;ModelCallStreamPart&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(),&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;});&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="k"&gt;return&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="na"&gt;messages&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;result&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;messages&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;};&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;This example demonstrates the core pattern:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;The workflow function is marked with &lt;code&gt;'use workflow'&lt;/code&gt;.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Tool implementations that need durable retries are marked with &lt;code&gt;'use step'&lt;/code&gt;.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;The report publishing tool requires human approval.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;The workflow can suspend and resume while waiting for the approval decision.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;p&gt;For a real deployment, the publishing operation should also implement server-controlled idempotency and authorization. The simple example focuses on the workflow integration rather than the complete business security layer.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h3&gt;


Step 4: Understand the difference between WorkflowAgent and ToolLoopAgent
&lt;/h3&gt;

&lt;div class="table-wrapper-paragraph"&gt;&lt;table&gt;
&lt;thead&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;th&gt;Feature&lt;/th&gt;
&lt;th&gt;ToolLoopAgent&lt;/th&gt;
&lt;th&gt;WorkflowAgent&lt;/th&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;/thead&gt;
&lt;tbody&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Execution&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;In-memory&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Durable workflow&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Process restart recovery&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;No automatic recovery&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Supported by runtime&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Tool retries&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Application-managed&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Per-step retry support&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Long approval waits&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Requires custom handling&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Durable suspension&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Tool execution visibility&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;AI SDK telemetry&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Workflow step visibility&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Streaming&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Direct stream consumption&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Workflow writable&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;/tbody&gt;
&lt;/table&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The recommended approach is not to replace every &lt;code&gt;ToolLoopAgent&lt;/code&gt; with &lt;code&gt;WorkflowAgent&lt;/code&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;For short, synchronous agent interactions, an in-memory agent is often simpler.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Use durable execution when the workflow needs to outlive its original request, survive process interruptions, wait for external events, or retry individual operations independently.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h3&gt;


Step 5: Make Chat Streaming Resumable
&lt;/h3&gt;

&lt;p&gt;One challenge in long-running AI applications is that the backend workflow and the frontend connection have different lifecycles.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;A user might:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Refresh the browser.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lose network connectivity.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Navigate away from a page.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Reconnect after a function timeout.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;p&gt;A durable workflow may still be running even though the original HTTP connection has disappeared.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;code&gt;WorkflowChatTransport&lt;/code&gt; provides a mechanism for resuming the chat stream using the workflow run ID and previously received stream chunks.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;A simplified client configuration:&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight tsx"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s1"&gt;use client&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="k"&gt;import&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;useChat&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;from&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s1"&gt;@ai-sdk/react&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="k"&gt;import&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;WorkflowChatTransport&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;from&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s1"&gt;@ai-sdk/workflow&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="k"&gt;import&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;useMemo&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;from&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s1"&gt;react&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="k"&gt;export&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;default&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kd"&gt;function&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;Chat&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;()&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="kd"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;transport&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;useMemo&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;()&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="k"&gt;new&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nc"&gt;WorkflowChatTransport&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;({&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="na"&gt;api&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s1"&gt;/api/chat&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="na"&gt;maxConsecutiveErrors&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="mi"&gt;5&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="na"&gt;initialStartIndex&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;-&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="mi"&gt;50&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;}),&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;[],&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;);&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="kd"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;messages&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;sendMessage&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;useChat&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;({&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="nx"&gt;transport&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;});&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="c1"&gt;// Render conversation and handle user input.&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;The server also needs the corresponding workflow stream endpoints.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;This is an important architectural detail: a durable backend does not automatically make the browser connection durable. The frontend needs a way to reconnect and retrieve the appropriate part of the workflow stream.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;References:&lt;/strong&gt; &lt;a href="https://vercel.com/kb/guide/what-is-workflowagent" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;Vercel — WorkflowAgent&lt;/a&gt; · &lt;a href="https://vercel.com/kb/guide/durableagent-to-workflowagent" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;AI SDK — WorkflowAgent Migration&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


7. LangGraph: Checkpointing and Interrupts
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;LangGraph approaches durable agent execution through graph state and persistence.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Its persistence architecture provides two complementary mechanisms:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Checkpointers&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Persist graph state for a specific thread.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;They support:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Conversation continuity&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Recovery from interruptions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Human-in-the-loop workflows&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Time travel&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Fault tolerance&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Stores&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Persist application-defined information across different threads.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;They are useful for:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;User preferences&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Long-term memory&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Shared knowledge&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Cross-conversation information&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;p&gt;A simplified configuration:&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight typescript"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="k"&gt;import&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="nx"&gt;MemorySaver&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="nx"&gt;StateGraph&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="nx"&gt;Annotation&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;from&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s1"&gt;@langchain/langgraph&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="kd"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;State&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;Annotation&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nc"&gt;Root&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;({&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="na"&gt;messages&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;Annotation&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="kr"&gt;string&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;[]&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;({&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="na"&gt;reducer&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;current&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;update&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;[&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;...&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;current&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;...&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;update&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;],&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="na"&gt;default&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;()&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;[],&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;}),&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;});&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="kd"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;builder&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;new&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nc"&gt;StateGraph&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;State&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;);&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="c1"&gt;// Add nodes and edges...&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="kd"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;checkpointer&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;new&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nc"&gt;MemorySaver&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;();&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="kd"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;graph&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;builder&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;compile&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;({&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="nx"&gt;checkpointer&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;});&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="kd"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;result&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;await&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;graph&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;invoke&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="na"&gt;messages&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;[&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s1"&gt;Analyze the requested document.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;],&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;},&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="na"&gt;configurable&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="na"&gt;thread_id&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s1"&gt;analysis-123&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;},&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;},&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;);&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;This example uses an in-memory checkpointer for illustration.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;It is not suitable for surviving process restarts. For production, use a persistent implementation such as PostgreSQL or another supported durable checkpointer.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h3&gt;


Human-in-the-loop with interrupts
&lt;/h3&gt;

&lt;p&gt;LangGraph provides the &lt;code&gt;interrupt()&lt;/code&gt; function to pause a graph and wait for external input.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Conceptually:&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight typescript"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="k"&gt;import&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="nx"&gt;interrupt&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="nx"&gt;Command&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;from&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s1"&gt;@langchain/langgraph&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="k"&gt;async&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kd"&gt;function&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;approvalNode&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;state&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="nl"&gt;proposedAction&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kr"&gt;string&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;})&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="kd"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;decision&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;interrupt&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;({&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="na"&gt;action&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;state&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;proposedAction&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="na"&gt;message&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s1"&gt;Approval is required.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;});&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="k"&gt;if &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;!&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;decision&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;approved&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="k"&gt;return&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="na"&gt;status&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s1"&gt;rejected&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;};&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="k"&gt;return&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="na"&gt;status&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s1"&gt;approved&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;};&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;The graph persists its state through its checkpointer.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Later, the application can resume the same thread using &lt;code&gt;Command&lt;/code&gt; with the user's response.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;This is useful for workflows where execution must pause for approval or additional input.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;One subtle but important implementation detail: when resuming an interrupted graph, the interrupted node may execute again from its beginning. Operations performed before &lt;code&gt;interrupt()&lt;/code&gt; therefore need to be designed carefully to avoid duplicate side effects.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;References:&lt;/strong&gt; &lt;a href="https://docs.langchain.com/oss/javascript/langgraph/persistence" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;LangGraph Persistence&lt;/a&gt; · &lt;a href="https://docs.langchain.com/oss/javascript/langgraph/interrupts" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;LangGraph Interrupts&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


8. Temporal: Durable Execution as an Infrastructure Primitive
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Temporal takes a different approach.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Rather than focusing specifically on agent state or conversation management, Temporal provides a general-purpose durable execution platform.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;It is designed for long-running, stateful workflows that need to survive failures.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Two concepts are particularly important:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Workflow&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Defines the orchestration logic and execution history.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Activity&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Performs external or non-deterministic operations such as API requests, database access, LLM calls, and file operations.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;A simplified AI workflow could look like this:&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight plaintext"&gt;&lt;code&gt;Temporal Workflow
|
v
Retrieve Context Activity
|
v
LLM Analysis Activity
|
v
Validation Activity
|
v
Wait for Approval Signal
|
v
Execute Business Operation
|
v
Complete
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;Temporal records workflow history and uses deterministic replay to reconstruct execution state.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;External interactions belong in Activities so their results can be recorded and reused during replay.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;This separation is fundamental.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;An LLM invocation should not be performed directly in a deterministic workflow definition. It should be executed as an Activity.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The same applies to database calls and external HTTP requests.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h3&gt;


When does Temporal make sense?
&lt;/h3&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Temporal is particularly relevant when:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Workflows span multiple services.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Tasks may run for hours or days.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong recovery requirements exist.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Human approval is part of the process.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Many independent workers execute tasks.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Workflow execution is critical to business operations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;p&gt;It also introduces additional infrastructure and operational responsibilities.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Teams need to understand workflow history, Activity retries, Worker deployment, workflow versioning, and task queue management.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;References:&lt;/strong&gt; &lt;a href="https://docs.temporal.io/ai" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;Temporal — Durable AI&lt;/a&gt; · &lt;a href="https://docs.temporal.io/develop/typescript" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;Temporal TypeScript SDK&lt;/a&gt; · &lt;a href="https://docs.temporal.io/workflow-definition" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;Temporal Workflow Determinism&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


9. Inngest and DBOS: Other Approaches Worth Evaluating
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Temporal and LangGraph are not the only options.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;For TypeScript-based applications, two other projects are worth considering.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h3&gt;


Inngest
&lt;/h3&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Inngest provides durable functions and agent workflows.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Its execution model is built around steps.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;For example:&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight typescript"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="k"&gt;import&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;inngest&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;from&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s1"&gt;./client&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="k"&gt;export&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kd"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;researchWorkflow&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;inngest&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;createFunction&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="na"&gt;id&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s1"&gt;research-workflow&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;},&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="k"&gt;async &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;({&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;event&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;step&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;})&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="kd"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;context&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;await&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;step&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;run&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s1"&gt;retrieve-context&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="k"&gt;async &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;()&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="k"&gt;return&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;retrieveContext&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;event&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;data&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;query&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;);&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;},&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;);&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="kd"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;analysis&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;await&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;step&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;run&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s1"&gt;generate-analysis&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="k"&gt;async &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;()&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="k"&gt;return&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;generateAnalysis&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;context&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;);&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;},&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;);&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="kd"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;report&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;await&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;step&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;run&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s1"&gt;validate-report&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="k"&gt;async &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;()&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="k"&gt;return&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;validateReport&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;analysis&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;);&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;},&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;);&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="k"&gt;return&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;report&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;},&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;);&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;The runtime checkpoints completed steps and resumes from the failed step when execution recovers.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Inngest also provides &lt;code&gt;step.waitForEvent()&lt;/code&gt; for human approvals and other external events.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Its durable agent approach goes further by treating each model call and tool call as a separately checkpointed step.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;This is useful when we want to write ordinary TypeScript functions instead of defining an explicit graph.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h3&gt;


DBOS
&lt;/h3&gt;

&lt;p&gt;DBOS provides durable execution for TypeScript and other languages, using a database-backed workflow model.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Its TypeScript SDK offers:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Workflow registration&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Durable steps&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Configurable retries&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Workflow IDs&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Idempotency and deduplication mechanisms&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Background execution&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Recovery after process restarts&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;p&gt;A simplified example:&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight typescript"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="k"&gt;import&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;DBOS&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;from&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s1"&gt;@dbos-inc/dbos-sdk&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="k"&gt;async&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kd"&gt;function&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;retrieveDocuments&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;()&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="c1"&gt;// External API or database operation&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="k"&gt;return&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;[&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s1"&gt;document-1&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s1"&gt;document-2&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;];&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="k"&gt;async&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kd"&gt;function&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;analyzeDocuments&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;()&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="c1"&gt;// LLM interaction&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="k"&gt;return&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="na"&gt;summary&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s1"&gt;Analysis completed&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;};&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="k"&gt;async&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kd"&gt;function&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;researchWorkflow&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;()&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="kd"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;documents&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;await&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;DBOS&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;runStep&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;()&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;retrieveDocuments&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(),&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="na"&gt;name&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s1"&gt;retrieve-documents&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="na"&gt;retriesAllowed&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kc"&gt;true&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="na"&gt;maxAttempts&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="mi"&gt;3&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;},&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;);&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="kd"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;analysis&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;await&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;DBOS&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;runStep&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;()&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;analyzeDocuments&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(),&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="na"&gt;name&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s1"&gt;analyze-documents&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="na"&gt;retriesAllowed&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kc"&gt;true&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="na"&gt;maxAttempts&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="mi"&gt;3&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;},&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;);&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="k"&gt;return&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="nx"&gt;documents&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="nx"&gt;analysis&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;};&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="kd"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;workflow&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;DBOS&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;registerWorkflow&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="nx"&gt;researchWorkflow&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;);&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;This example shows the basic step model. A production application must initialize DBOS, register the workflow, and configure its database and worker lifecycle.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;DBOS also requires deterministic workflow code and appropriate serialization of workflow inputs and outputs.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h3&gt;


How do these approaches compare?
&lt;/h3&gt;

&lt;div class="table-wrapper-paragraph"&gt;&lt;table&gt;
&lt;thead&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;th&gt;Technology&lt;/th&gt;
&lt;th&gt;Main strength&lt;/th&gt;
&lt;th&gt;Best suited for&lt;/th&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;/thead&gt;
&lt;tbody&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;LangGraph&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Graph state and checkpointing&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Stateful agent workflows&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Temporal&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;General-purpose durable execution&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Complex distributed business processes&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Inngest&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Durable TypeScript functions and agents&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Event-driven agent workflows&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;DBOS&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Database-backed durable execution&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;TypeScript applications needing durable steps&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Vercel Workflow + WorkflowAgent&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Native AI SDK integration&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Durable agents in Vercel-based applications&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;/tbody&gt;
&lt;/table&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;p&gt;There is no universally correct choice.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The right decision depends on the execution model, deployment environment, workflow duration, infrastructure constraints, and the level of operational control required.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;References:&lt;/strong&gt; &lt;a href="https://www.inngest.com/docs/durable-execution/durable-agents" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;Inngest Durable Agents&lt;/a&gt; · &lt;a href="https://docs.dbos.dev/typescript/tutorials/workflow-tutorial" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;DBOS TypeScript Workflows&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


10. Designing a Production-Ready Agent Workflow
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Choosing a durable execution framework is only one part of the solution.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;We also need to design the workflow itself.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Let's consider a document analysis and approval workflow.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The system should:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;ol&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Receive a document.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Extract its content.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Analyze the information.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Generate a proposed report.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Wait for human approval.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Publish the approved report.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Store the final result.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ol&gt;

&lt;p&gt;A possible architecture:&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight plaintext"&gt;&lt;code&gt;             User
|
v
AI Application
|
v
Workflow Runtime
|
+-------+--------+
|                |
v                v
Extract Step    Analysis Step
|                |
v                v
Storage          LLM / Tools
|                |
+--------+-------+
|
v
Validation Step
|
v
Approval Required
|
+------+------+
|             |
Reject        Approve
|             |
v             v
Stop      Publish Step
|
v
Save Result
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;Several design decisions matter here.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h3&gt;


Persist the right information
&lt;/h3&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Do not put every document, model response, or binary object into the workflow's event history.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Use references to external storage for large payloads.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Persist only the data required to recover the next step.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h3&gt;


Separate planning from execution
&lt;/h3&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The LLM may decide which operation should happen next, but the runtime should control which operations are actually executed.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The agent should not own unrestricted workflow persistence or authorization decisions.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h3&gt;


Define explicit failure boundaries
&lt;/h3&gt;

&lt;p&gt;A document extraction failure should not necessarily require the analysis to restart.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;An approval timeout should not cause the document to be processed again.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;A publishing failure should not require repeating the original LLM request.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Each operation should have a clear recovery strategy.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h3&gt;


Keep business state authoritative
&lt;/h3&gt;

&lt;p&gt;A workflow checkpoint records execution progress.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;It should not replace the authoritative transaction state of the business system.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;For example, an approval workflow may persist its state in the orchestration engine, but the actual transaction should be committed and recorded in the relevant business system.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h3&gt;


Make workflows version-aware
&lt;/h3&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Long-running workflows can remain active across application deployments.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;A workflow that started using one version of the code may resume after a newer version has been deployed.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Changing step ordering, workflow logic, or serialized state formats can break recovery if compatibility is not considered.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Workflow versioning, migration strategies, and backward-compatible payloads should be part of the deployment design.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


11. Common Mistakes in Durable Agent Implementations
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;There are a few mistakes I would specifically avoid.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;1. Treating conversation history as workflow state&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Saving messages does not mean the agent can resume from the exact point where it stopped.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;2. Retrying everything&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;A failed tool should not force all previous model calls and tool executions to run again.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Retry boundaries should be explicit.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;3. Assuming exactly-once side effects&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;A durable workflow cannot automatically guarantee exactly-once behavior across arbitrary external services.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Use idempotency keys, deduplication, and reconciliation.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;4. Storing large payloads inside checkpoints&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Store references to documents and large artifacts instead of repeatedly serializing them.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;5. Ignoring workflow versioning&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;A long-running workflow may outlive multiple application deployments.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Plan how in-flight executions will behave when code changes.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;6. Keeping workers alive while waiting for approval&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;A durable wait should suspend execution and release the worker rather than holding a process open.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;7. Using durable execution for every interaction&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;A simple question-answering endpoint does not necessarily need a workflow engine.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The added infrastructure should solve an actual reliability problem.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;8. Confusing agent reasoning with business authorization&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;An agent deciding to perform an action does not mean that action is authorized.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Sensitive operations must be validated and approved by trusted application logic.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


12. What Can an AI Chapter Lead Contribute?
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;I believe durable execution is particularly important when multiple teams are building AI-powered features within the same organization.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Without shared patterns, each team may implement its own persistence, retry logic, background execution, and approval mechanisms.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;This creates duplicated engineering effort and inconsistent reliability.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;There are several practical areas where an AI Chapter Lead can contribute.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h3&gt;


1. Establish a Common Durable Execution Pattern
&lt;/h3&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Define when an agent should run in memory and when it should run inside a durable workflow.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;For example:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="table-wrapper-paragraph"&gt;&lt;table&gt;
&lt;thead&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;th&gt;Use case&lt;/th&gt;
&lt;th&gt;Recommended approach&lt;/th&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;/thead&gt;
&lt;tbody&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Simple chat response&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;In-memory agent&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Short tool interaction&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Standard agent with controlled retries&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Multi-step background task&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Durable workflow&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Human approval&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Durable wait and resume&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Long-running research&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Durable agent&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Cross-service business process&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Workflow engine&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Independent subagent tasks&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Durable child workflows or delegated executions&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;/tbody&gt;
&lt;/table&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;p&gt;This prevents unnecessary infrastructure while ensuring that critical workflows have appropriate recovery mechanisms.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h3&gt;


2. Build a Shared Workflow Abstraction
&lt;/h3&gt;

&lt;p&gt;We can create a reusable internal package that provides:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Workflow lifecycle management&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Checkpoint persistence&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Standard retry policies&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Idempotency helpers&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Cancellation support&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Human approval mechanisms&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Execution state management&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Observability integration&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Teams should not need to implement these capabilities independently.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;However, shared abstractions should not hide framework-specific behavior that affects reliability.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h3&gt;


3. Define Standard Retry and Recovery Policies
&lt;/h3&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Not every failure should trigger another attempt.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;For example:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="table-wrapper-paragraph"&gt;&lt;table&gt;
&lt;thead&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;th&gt;Failure&lt;/th&gt;
&lt;th&gt;Strategy&lt;/th&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;/thead&gt;
&lt;tbody&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Temporary network failure&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Retry with backoff&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Provider rate limit&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Respect retry guidance and budget&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Invalid model output&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Validate and optionally regenerate&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Authorization failure&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Stop and escalate&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Invalid tool arguments&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Correct or request clarification&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Business rule violation&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Stop or request human review&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;External operation timeout&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Reconcile before retrying&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;/tbody&gt;
&lt;/table&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;p&gt;We can define common retry budgets, deadlines, maximum attempts, and error classification rules.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;This reduces inconsistent failure handling across applications.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h3&gt;


4. Establish Idempotency Standards
&lt;/h3&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Every operation that creates an external side effect should have an explicit idempotency strategy.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;For example:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Database writes&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Report publishing&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Email sending&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;External API requests&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Business transaction execution&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Agent-to-agent task submission&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;p&gt;This is especially important when workflows involve retries or uncertain execution outcomes.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h3&gt;


5. Standardize Human Approval
&lt;/h3&gt;

&lt;p&gt;We can establish a shared approval model that defines:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Who can approve an action.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Which operations require approval.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;How approval requests are stored.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;How decisions are associated with workflow executions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;What happens when approval expires.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;How rejected actions are handled.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;How approval decisions are audited.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;p&gt;This makes human-in-the-loop workflows consistent across teams.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h3&gt;


6. Build a Reference Implementation
&lt;/h3&gt;

&lt;p&gt;A practical internal example should demonstrate:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;ol&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Durable agent execution.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Step-level checkpointing.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Independent retries.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Human approval.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Resume after application restart.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Idempotent external operations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Distributed tracing.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Workflow versioning.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ol&gt;

&lt;p&gt;This is more useful than a standalone demo that only shows a successful agent response.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h3&gt;


7. Measure Reliability
&lt;/h3&gt;

&lt;p&gt;We should define measurable outcomes.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Useful metrics include:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Workflow completion rate&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Recovery success rate&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Number of repeated model calls&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Duplicate side-effect attempts&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Approval wait duration&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Retry count per workflow&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Average workflow duration&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Cost per successful workflow&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Human escalation rate&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The objective should be to understand whether durable execution actually improves reliability without creating unnecessary complexity.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


13. When Should We Adopt Durable Execution?
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;A durable execution framework is particularly valuable when:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A task involves multiple dependent operations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Execution can exceed HTTP request timeouts.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A workflow must survive process restarts.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Expensive model calls should not be repeated unnecessarily.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A human may need to approve an operation later.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;The agent interacts with external systems that may fail independently.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Multiple workers or services participate in one business process.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;p&gt;For a short chat response, a regular AI SDK agent may be sufficient.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;For a multi-hour research workflow or a business operation that cannot be safely restarted from the beginning, durable execution becomes much more important.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The correct architecture is the simplest one that provides the required failure guarantees.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


Conclusion
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;AI agents are becoming more capable, but greater capability introduces additional operational complexity.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;An agent that can call tools, delegate tasks, and interact with external systems must also be able to recover from failures, preserve execution progress, and handle interruptions safely.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Durable execution provides the foundation for this.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Checkpointing preserves progress. Retries recover from transient failures. Idempotency prevents duplicate side effects. Durable waits enable human approval without keeping workers occupied. Workflow versioning allows long-running executions to survive application changes.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;For AI engineering teams, the goal should not be to make every agent use a workflow engine.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;It should be to identify which operations require durability and apply the right execution model to them.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;My recommendation:&lt;/strong&gt; Start with one multi-step workflow that includes an external API call and a human approval step. Implement it with a durable execution framework, simulate process failures, and verify that completed work is not repeated and external side effects are not duplicated.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;A production-ready agent is not one that only works when everything goes right.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;It is one that knows how to recover when things go wrong.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;




